,"value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-13T06:16:29-07:00","id":1374555,"title":"","content":"Is there a limit in the number of specialities a character can have on a single skill?<br /> <br /> I was treating as 1 per skill, but there is always that character with 7 PhDs...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-07T11:13:17-07:00","id":1379282,"title":"","content":"Is the prerequisite for the Adaptation Mega-Edge really Mega-Stamina 3 or is it a mistake? Neither the Robot Antagonist nor the Warper Nova Archetype has Mega-Stamina 3, but they still have Adaptation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>When will you rage?","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1405-anteros","name":"Anteros","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1405_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"661"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-07T12:34:52-07:00","id":1379298,"title":"","content":"<br /> When crafting Super Science Items; are devices that mimic Superior Powers considered Advanced Science, Inspired Science, or Powered Science?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#181818\"><span style=\"font-family:Merriweather\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">\u201cHumpty had always sat on walls, it was his way.\u201d </span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#181818\"><span style=\"font-family:Merriweather\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">\u2015 </span></span></span><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Lato\"><b><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Jasper Fforde, </span></b></span></span><span style=\"color:#181818\"><span style=\"font-family:Merriweather\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://www.goodreads.com/work/quotes/2504943\" target=\"_blank\">The Big Over Easy</a></span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1756-mythadvocate","name":"MythAdvocate","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1756_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"444"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-07T12:36:01-07:00","id":1379299,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Anteros</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1362003-ask-a-dev?p=1379282#post1379282\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is the prerequisite for the Adaptation Mega-Edge really Mega-Stamina 3 or is it a mistake? Neither the Robot Antagonist nor the Warper Nova Archetype has Mega-Stamina 3, but they still have Adaptation.</div> </div> </div> </div>they\u2019ve put a hold on Aberrant mechanics questions because it\u2019s in the process of mechanics revisions.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-12T17:41:27-07:00","id":1380803,"title":"","content":"Do Psiads have to worry about Psionic Dysfunction or is this a Psion only thing due to the whole single Aptitude element function of the Prometheus Chamber. <br /> <br /> Cause if not I could totally see a psiad with say a high Adaptation Biokinesis Mode but say a low Transmogrify if they aren't super into changing their physical form.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/661-lordheru","name":"LordHeru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar661_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-12T18:00:57-07:00","id":1380810,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LordHeru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1362003-ask-a-dev?p=1380803#post1380803\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do Psiads have to worry about Psionic Dysfunction or is this a Psion only thing due to the whole single Aptitude element function of the Prometheus Chamber. <br /> <br /> Cause if not I could totally see a psiad with say a high Adaptation Biokinesis Mode but say a low Transmogrify if they aren't super into changing their physical form.</div> </div> </div> </div>They do, but mechanically it\u2019s very difficult for a psiad to get Dysfunction as they count Mode dots across Aptitudes when checking for it. As you start with at least one dot in several Modes, you\u2019d have to take Strong Mode in a primary so you can push that up to a potential 4 dots, then raise that Mode to max while keeping everything else at one dot. It\u2019s possible, but it takes considerable effort from the player to make it happen.<br /> <br /> Dysfunction is more of a problem for psions because they\u2019ve been artificially limited and can\u2019t balance their psionic potential across the spectrum of Aptitudes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-15T02:58:20-07:00","id":1381579,"title":"","content":"Which Teleportation mode dots are required to Teleport a spaceship and it's inhabitants, assuming it is not a jump ship?<br /> <br /> I'm guessing Translocation 4 (Long Jump) &amp; Transmassion 3 (Transmit Mass) at a minimum, but I can see a case for Transmassion 4 (Transmit Person) or Transportal 5 (Warp).<br /> <br /> Trying to figure how non-jumpships travel interstellar.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-15T03:23:53-07:00","id":1381585,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>FallenEco</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1362003-ask-a-dev?p=1381579#post1381579\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Which Teleportation mode dots are required to Teleport a spaceship and it's inhabitants, assuming it is not a jump ship?<br /> <br /> I'm guessing Translocation 4 (Long Jump) &amp; Transmassion 3 (Transmit Mass) at a minimum, but I can see a case for Transmassion 4 (Transmit Person) or Transportal 5 (Warp).<br /> <br /> Trying to figure how non-jumpships travel interstellar.</div> </div> </div> </div>Transmassion 4 is the main choice to send a ship and passengers. Transportal 4 is an alternative for smaller vessels, or multiple of smaller vessels while you keep the portal open.<br /> <br /> You don\u2019t need anything from Translocation for moving objects or other people, unless you want to accompany them.<br /> <br /> The most \u2018common\u2019 way for non jump ships to interstellar travel is to install a Teleportation Helm, then the teleporter just needs Transmassion 4 to accompany, not Translocation *and* Transmassion.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":156,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","user":"Bunyip","date":". 04-15-2020, 06:27 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-27T03:02:34-07:00","id":1384137,"title":"","content":"I'm really enjoying the new systems but I have a number of questions:<br /> <br /> <b>Trinity Continuum</b><br /> <br /> <u>One</u><br /> <br /> Is it correct that the maximum number of Injury Conditions that can be inflicted in a single same-Scale attack is two (one from Inflict Injury and one from Critical)?<br /> <br /> <u>Two</u><br /> <br /> p. 104: &quot;Shove (Variable successes): For every one success you spend after beating the Difficulty ...&quot;<br /> <br /> There is no Difficulty stipulated for the Stunt. Should this be worded more like Feint (&quot;For every success spent on...&quot;)? <br /> <br /> <u>Three</u><br /> <br /> p. 112: &quot;... a character can only deal damage to a target no greater than three Scale above her ...&quot;. <br /> <br /> As written, this means that a Scale 1 character can deal damage to a Scale 4 character. That seems inconsistent with other statements in the various books. Is it an error?<br /> <br /> <u>Four</u><br /> <br /> p. 113 - 114: &quot;Fin\u2019s Defense is 2 against the attack ... [Ariadne] uses the first two successes to overcome the Difficulty (Defense of 1, so Difficulty 1) ...&quot;<br /> <br /> This seems to suggest that you need to spend a success beyond the Difficulty to overcome it. Are the numbers in the parentheses an error?<br /> <br /> <u>Five</u><br /> <br /> p. 125: [Chart of example weapons].<br /> <br /> Is the Enhancement rating shown in the chart pre- or post-tag effects?<br /> <br /> If the latter, is the Enhancement of the Assault Rifle or the Katana recorded incorrectly?<br /> <br /> <b>Aeon</b><br /> <br /> <u>One</u><br /> <br /> p. 207: &quot;Psions can also combine their abilities to take advantage of each Aptitude\u2019s specialties and open new ways to use their powers ...&quot;<br /> <br /> Is it correct that psions cannot enjoy a similar benefit from combining their Aptitude and Auxiliary Modes?<br /> <br /> Relatedly, are psiads able to enjoy this benefit by combining their multiple Aptitudes? For example, could a Biokinetic/Vitakinetic psiad access the noetic template of others to shapeshift them?<br /> <br /> <u>Two</u><br /> <br /> p. 209: &quot;[Proxy-tier psions] can also learn their Aptitude\u2019s single seven-dot power.&quot;<br /> <br /> Does an Aptitude's seven-dot power count as a dot for the purposes of every Mode of an Aptitude (for calculating how long effects last, etc.)?<br /> <br /> <u>Three</u><br /> <br /> p. 210: &quot;Form Mastery ... The player crafts her desired shape from the various Transmogrification powers available to the character ...&quot;<br /> <br /> This suggests that Form Mastery only applies to the effects of powers from the Transmogrify Mode (and not Adaptation or Psychomorphing). Is that the intention?<br /> <br /> <u>Four</u><br /> <br /> p. 215: &quot;Chimera ... the psion can make any biokinetic alternations permanent ...&quot;<br /> <br /> This suggests that the effects of any Biokinesis power can be made permanent (including Adaptation and Psychomorphing)? Is that the intention?<br /> <br /> <u>Five</u><br /> <br /> p. 216: &quot;Fleshcrafter ... he may spend an additional Psi point to increase the Scale of one aspect of the power, like Speed Scale, by one ...&quot;<br /> <br /> Is it correct that a psion can only spend a single Psi point when using this power (or the analogous six-dot powers of other Aptitudes)?<br /> <br /> In either case, could Fleshcrafter be used with Enhance or Perfection to give the psion strength Scale 2?<br /> <br /> <u>Six</u><br /> <br /> p. 253: &quot;Astral Life ... This power can be combined with Division to allow the psion\u2019s astral form to possess someone else\u2019s body.&quot;<br /> <br /> This suggests (to me) that the user of Astral Life can utilise a more profound form of possession, that lasts Psi x weeks per success. Is that the intention?<br /> <br /> If so, does the psion also use the reduced target number for &quot;copy[ing] her mental template onto the victim&quot;?<br /> <br /> <u>Seven</u><br /> <br /> p. 275: &quot;Poison (Non-Lethal) ... causes the Unconscious Status Condition ...&quot;<br /> <br /> The Unconscious Status Condition lasts a number of rounds (or minutes outside of combat) based on the damage source. What is the &quot;damage source&quot; for this weapon tag?<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1562-fikealox","name":"Fikealox","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"85"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-27T03:06:24-07:00","id":1384139,"title":"","content":"Thanks in advance for your answers. Sorry about the long post. I tried to make all the questions easy to answer.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1562-fikealox","name":"Fikealox","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"85"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-27T05:11:23-07:00","id":1384168,"title":"","content":"Okay... lots of questions. Let\u2019s see how we go.<br /> <br /> Trinity Continuum Core<br /> 1 - Yes<br /> 2 - Difficulty is Defense. You need to lay hands on a person to shove them, whereas you can spend successes on Feint to help allies if you haven\u2019t overcome the target\u2019s Defense.<br /> 3 - I don\u2019t believe it is an error, can you point to the \u2018statements in the various books\u2019?<br /> 4 - Yes, oops. Fin\u2019s Defense is 2 and Ariadne has 3 successes - she spends 2 to deal with Defense 2 and has 1 left over. If Fin has no Soft Armor Ariadne inflicts injury and still has 1 success to spend.<br /> 5 - Post-tags, and Assault Rifle appears to be correct. Note that Tags that give Enhancement in certain situations (Two-Handed\u2019s +1 Enhancement to <i>Inflict Injury</i>) aren\u2019t included in the blanket Enhancement for the weapon. Katana does seem to be miscalculated - it should be Enhancement 2, or Quality 3. Quality 3 is probably what they\u2019re going for.<br /> <br /> AEon<br /> <br /> 1a - Correct, you can\u2019t combine with Auxiliary Modes.<br /> 1b - Psiads can combine their own Aptitudes for effects, not for the boosts psions get. In other words, yes, a BK/VK psiad can shapeshift others, but they don\u2019t get the p.208 bonuses for psions combining Aptitudes.<br /> 2 - Yes.<br /> 3 &amp; 4 - Funnily enough, both say the opposite of the intention. For Form Mastery you can craft other BK effects into the form and pay XP as normal. For Chimera the biokinetic can only make Transmogrify changes permanent.<br /> 5a - The BK can only spend a single psi point per aspect. She could spend one to increase Speed Scale, and another to increase Might or Size Scale. This applies to the 6-dot powers for all Aptitudes.<br /> 5b - Yes. Proxy-tier characters can be scary.<br /> 6a - Kind of. Division has advantages over Possession, but Possession has a few advantages of its own that Division doesn\u2019t have.<br /> 6b - I\u2019d say yes.<br /> 7 - Not sure. I\u2019d look at how much damage the attack would have caused if it was an injuring attack. Usually 1 but maybe more if the successes could have purchased Critical.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-27T12:27:12-07:00","id":1384239,"title":"","content":"Thanks so much, for the quick and comprehensive answers, Bunyip. I hope it wasn't too arduous.<br /> <br /> With respect to question 3, the statements I was thinking of were:<ul><li>Trinity Continuum, p. 112: &quot;In the case where there is an encounter between individuals of differing Scale, the entity with three or more Scale above the other dictates the results of the conflict.&quot;</li> <li>While I do not have a copy, I believe the Aberrant Kickstarter manuscript says something virtually identical, though framed in terms of the higher-Scale character &quot;automatically succeeding&quot;.</li> </ul><br /> On my reading, the passage I cited in question 3 suggests that a Scale 1 character automatically loses only against a Scale 5+ character, while these other passages suggest that a Scale 1 character always loses against a Scale 4+ character.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1562-fikealox","name":"Fikealox","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"85"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-18T17:11:17-07:00","id":1389791,"title":"","content":"So, I know this one is still a ways out, but I was curious if there had been any spoilers or teasers about Aegis released?<br /> <br /> If not, could you give us the elevator pitch for it, maybe? Or even just the rough historical period (I was thinking hellenistic greece, but I\u2019m not sure that\u2019s been confirmed)?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-18T18:50:35-07:00","id":1389817,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BrilliantRain</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1362003-ask-a-dev?p=1389791#post1389791\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, I know this one is still a ways out, but I was curious if there had been any spoilers or teasers about Aegis released?</div> </div> </div> </div>Until and unless it's given an official announcement, it's just wishful thinking.<br /> <br /> Major projects currently in development:<br /> <br /> - Adventure!<br /> - Assassins<br /> - Aberrant<br /> - Anima","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#800000\">Ian A. A. Watson</span></b><span style=\"color:#bdc3c7\">(he/she)</span><br /> <b>Onyx Path Community Manager<br /> Trinity Continuum Content Lead</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4-ianwatson","name":"IanWatson","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4_2.png","title":"Community Manager","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1512"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-26T11:42:15-07:00","id":1391735,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>IanWatson</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1362003-ask-a-dev?p=1389817#post1389817\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Until and unless it's given an official announcement, it's just wishful thinking.<br /> <br /> Major projects currently in development:<br /> <br /> - Adventure!<br /> - Assassins<br /> - Aberrant<br /> - Anima</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks for the answer. I\u2019ll definitely keep an eye out for any future announcements.<br /> <br /> A couple of questions for things you are definitely working on then.<br /> <br /> Can a Nova build an enhanced item without actually understanding how it works? Like, if a Nova wanted a cloak of invisibility, could they just try to \u201cimpress\u201d their power on a piece of fabric, or would they need to do something scientific, such as reweaving it out of complex meta-materials with a negative refractive index?<br /> <br /> Will the new edition of Adventure! go into what happened to all the \u201cweird science\u201d and \u201cstrange locations\u201d after the Hammersmith Effect finally wears off? If nothing else, I\u2019d enjoy knowing what happened to Enkidu and his people, because they don\u2019t seem to be around later.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-09T06:28:20-07:00","id":1395331,"title":"","content":"How is Energetics 1 (Conversion) intended to function against attacks? It only uses the mechanical language of indirect damage like environmental effects (\u201clevels of damage\u201d). If you were to apply those mechanics to direct attacks it would be an incredibly powerful defense because it wouldn\u2019t block attack successes like soft armor it would block purchases of inflict injury and critical. Even a starting character focused on Energetics could shrug off higher scale attacks, basically turn an aberrant\u2019s scale 3 laser blast into a \u201cwomp womp womp\u201d sad horn noise. Hilarious, but seems broken.<br /> <br /> <br /> Will there be an errata for Trinity and \u00c6on like Scion got, or at least an FAQ?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24935-werlynn","name":"werlynn","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"192"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-10T22:23:02-07:00","id":1395764,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>werlynn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1362003-ask-a-dev?p=1395331#post1395331\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Will there be an errata for Trinity and \u00c6on like Scion got, or at least an FAQ?</div> </div> </div> </div>Trinity Continuum and Scion both had the same errata process. Basically:<br /> 1. Backer PDF goes out<br /> 2. Errata are collected<br /> 3. Errata are incorporated into the text<br /> 4. Final PDF/physical book goes out<br /> <br /> Something happened in Scion's third step where, although errata were collected, an earlier un-errata'd version of the text was published. So we released a separate errata document by way of apology and to account for those changes.<br /> <br /> That didn't happen with the Trinity Continuum book. The changes we made were incorporated into the final book. So there's no need for us to have a separate errata document.<br /> <br /> An FAQ is a possibility, but I don't see sufficient need for one at the moment.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#800000\">Ian A. A. Watson</span></b><span style=\"color:#bdc3c7\">(he/she)</span><br /> <b>Onyx Path Community Manager<br /> Trinity Continuum Content Lead</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4-ianwatson","name":"IanWatson","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4_2.png","title":"Community Manager","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1512"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-11T04:34:09-07:00","id":1395808,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>werlynn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1362003-ask-a-dev?p=1395331#post1395331\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How is Energetics 1 (Conversion) intended to function against attacks?</div> </div> </div> </div>After rolling to activate the power (and spending 1 Psi point if activating reflexively) the psion selects up to Mode dots/2 types of energy (or attack \u2018energies\u2019 from the power description) and spends successes up to Mode dots/2 (per energy type) to subtract that number of successes from attacks of that type - in effect, increasing the Difficulty/Defense against those attack types.<br /> <br /> This applies to the selected energy types within the character\u2019s Radius and lasts for one scene. Note that this is an imprecise power that applies against the energy type regardless of source - if the character chooses to reduce laser energy and then fires her own laser pistol it will also be affected as her power transforms the coherent light into something else.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-19T01:56:56-07:00","id":1403500,"title":"","content":"Hello all!<br /> <br /> A couple of questions:<br /> <br /> 1) Regarding vehicles have a cost that is calculated according to the tags they have.<br /> In the table on page 128 in the Core Rulebook, some vehicles are extremely expensive and are marked with an &quot;L&quot; as a cost and require the character to have the Loaded Enhanced Edge.<br /> <br /> But if I am building a vehicle, how expensive must it be to get an L cost? How many dots in tags must it have?<br /> <br /> 2) Target number in all rolls is set according to the character tier, as a standard, let's assume 8.<br /> The difficulty to overcome in a roll is the number of dice that roll an 8 or higher.<br /> But an 8 is a tough roll, so is it expected to have most of the difficulties set to 1? Is there anywhere examples of difficulties, when should I require more than one successful roll?<br /> <br /> Thanks!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26301-sothus","name":"Sothus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26301_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":1,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"15"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-19T04:42:39-07:00","id":1403510,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sothus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1362003-ask-a-dev?p=1403500#post1403500\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1) Regarding vehicles have a cost that is calculated according to the tags they have.<br /> In the table on page 128 in the Core Rulebook, some vehicles are extremely expensive and are marked with an &quot;L&quot; as a cost and require the character to have the Loaded Enhanced Edge.<br /> <br /> But if I am building a vehicle, how expensive must it be to get an L cost? How many dots in tags must it have?</div> </div> </div> </div>You need the Loaded Enhanced Edge (Core p. 67) to afford items with an \u2018L\u2019 cost. Vehicles with L cost can have 7 points of positive tags (Core p. 128).<br /> <br /> Vehicles can have up to their Wealth cost in positive tags (Core p. 127), so a vehicle with 6 or 7 points of tags has the L cost.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sothus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1362003-ask-a-dev?p=1403500#post1403500\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> 2) Target number in all rolls is set according to the character tier, as a standard, let's assume 8.<br /> The difficulty to overcome in a roll is the number of dice that roll an 8 or higher.<br /> But an 8 is a tough roll, so is it expected to have most of the difficulties set to 1? Is there anywhere examples of difficulties, when should I require more than one successful roll?</div> </div> </div> </div>Many, yes, but most? Depends on the game. <br /> <br /> Many types of rolls in the action/procedural/intrigue systems include associated Difficulties. For setting other DiffIculties, the table on p. 71 is for Enhancement but gives reasonable descriptive levels to help relate to numerical ones.<br /> <br /> In general, you\u2019ll want at least three dice to hit the probability for getting at least one success. Don\u2019t forget that characters often have Enhancement as well, and you only need one rolled success for the Enhancement to add to it to overcome Difficulty or Complications.<br /> <br /> Edit to add: It\u2019s worth noting that Storypath is built around the idea of players not having to roll unless there\u2019s a reasonable chance of failure, and it\u2019s dramatically interesting. Storypath characters are competent action heroes so if you\u2019re coming at the game from a past expectation of rolling for everything, set aside that habit. Use the 3 to 1 guide to help with what characters can do. If a character has a pool of 6 dice, some Enhancement, and the Difficulty is only 1 or 2, don\u2019t bother rolling unless there\u2019s a lot riding on the success or failure of that roll Similarly if they have 3-4 dice and it\u2019s a simply Difficulty 1 roll. Unless it matters if the character fails, let them succeed and move on.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":156,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","user":"Bunyip","date":". 07-19-2020, 07:48 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-20T11:38:30-07:00","id":1403693,"title":"","content":"I feel like there\u2019s a fair amount going on with the Trinity Continuum system that could be usefully unpacked and dissected. Have you guys considered doing a Storyguide book for it, especially now that you\u2019ve gotten to make modifications to the system and run it through a nice shakedown process?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-22T12:01:40-07:00","id":1404067,"title":"","content":"So, I know you guys aren\u2019t really answering Aberrant questions right now, but, as I was wondering something that was more setting related, I thought that might be alright?<br /> <br /> Anyway.<br /> <br /> I looked in the backer manuscript and, while it discusses particular eruptions, it never really discusses eruptions in general, what that feels like, and just how dangerous/obvious it could/should be. So, I was curious if there are any suggested particular limits around eruption. Can someone simply \u201cease\u201d through without really even noticing? Can someone without any energy related powers still have an \u201cexplosive\u201d eruption?<br /> <br /> How much can someone\u2019s body change without buying powers/mutations to represent that? Like, if a character had not been strong before, could they buy increased Might because of their eruption, even without getting Mega-Might? Could you justify buying Edges like Striking without necessarily taking Mega-Attributes when you erupted? Could you have changes that were effectively \u201ccosmetic\u201d without needing to have a Transformation or a power like Morph? Could someone with gender dysphoria subconsciously \u201creassign\u201d themselves during the eruption or would taking specific powers be recommended for that? Could various physical issues be spontaneously healed during an eruption without the Nova having regenerative powers afterward?<br /> <br /> Even if this is more of a table level decision, it might be worth a text box or something in the chargen chapter to give people some ideas for where the limits are, if any.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-25T07:44:00-07:00","id":1404591,"title":"","content":"Hello again!<br /> <br /> An AEon question... in page 207 it is stated that a psion can combine multiple modes. Should we treat that as a mixed action, in order to determine what to roll?<br /> <br /> Thanks!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26301-sothus","name":"Sothus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26301_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":1,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"15"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-25T09:50:52-07:00","id":1404596,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BrilliantRain</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1362003-ask-a-dev?p=1404067#post1404067\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, I know you guys aren\u2019t really answering Aberrant questions right now, but, as I was wondering something that was more setting related, I thought that might be alright?<br /> <br /> Anyway.<br /> <br /> I looked in the backer manuscript and, while it discusses particular eruptions, it never really discusses eruptions in general, what that feels like, and just how dangerous/obvious it could/should be. So, I was curious if there are any suggested particular limits around eruption. Can someone simply \u201cease\u201d through without really even noticing? Can someone without any energy related powers still have an \u201cexplosive\u201d eruption?<br /> <br /> How much can someone\u2019s body change without buying powers/mutations to represent that? Like, if a character had not been strong before, could they buy increased Might because of their eruption, even without getting Mega-Might? Could you justify buying Edges like Striking without necessarily taking Mega-Attributes when you erupted? Could you have changes that were effectively \u201ccosmetic\u201d without needing to have a Transformation or a power like Morph? Could someone with gender dysphoria subconsciously \u201creassign\u201d themselves during the eruption or would taking specific powers be recommended for that? Could various physical issues be spontaneously healed during an eruption without the Nova having regenerative powers afterward?<br /> <br /> Even if this is more of a table level decision, it might be worth a text box or something in the chargen chapter to give people some ideas for where the limits are, if any.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's intentionally vague. Whatever works for your table.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#800000\">Ian A. A. Watson</span></b><span style=\"color:#bdc3c7\">(he/she)</span><br /> <b>Onyx Path Community Manager<br /> Trinity Continuum Content Lead</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4-ianwatson","name":"IanWatson","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4_2.png","title":"Community Manager","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1512"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-25T14:48:26-07:00","id":1404644,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sothus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1362003-ask-a-dev?p=1404591#post1404591\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hello again!<br /> <br /> An AEon question... in page 207 it is stated that a psion can combine multiple modes. Should we treat that as a mixed action, in order to determine what to roll?<br /> <br /> Thanks!</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, this is a mixed action.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-27T11:28:09-07:00","id":1404948,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>IanWatson</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1362003-ask-a-dev?p=1404596#post1404596\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It's intentionally vague. Whatever works for your table.</div> </div> </div> </div>Adding a text box to that effect in the chargen section might be useful, just to give everyone permission to have Eruption do whatever they need it to do.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-02T01:33:08-07:00","id":1405898,"title":"","content":"Blink (Teleportation Translocation 1) describe a stunt in a way I don\u2019t understand exactly what to do.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Blink: Like the Dodge Stunt, the Translocation + Psi roll generates successes, which an opponent must overcome in order to inflict an Injury. The character teleports no more than a single range band and always either teleports away from an opponent or behind cover, whichever option is most obviously effective. </div> </div> </div>Do I roll Mode+Psi instead of regular defense or do I add it to the regular defense roll when using this stunt? How much does this stunt cost?<br /> Thnaks!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-02T03:02:49-07:00","id":1405903,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mateus Luz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1362003-ask-a-dev?p=1405898#post1405898\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Blink (Teleportation Translocation 1) describe a stunt in a way I don\u2019t understand exactly what to do.<br /> <br /> Do I roll Mode+Psi instead of regular defense or do I add it to the regular defense roll when using this stunt? How much does this stunt cost?<br /> Thnaks!</div> </div> </div> </div>You activate the Blink power as per standard Psi power rules - rolling Psi + Translocation as an ordinary action. This gives you your successes that you add to your Defense for subsequent attacks. Whether the opponent hits or not, Blink then teleports you away. <br /> <br /> When using Blink as your Defense stunt you don\u2019t get to roll a Resilience Attribute as well - you\u2019re either relying on psi or your own body.<br /> <br /> I\u2019m not sure what you mean by how much does it cost.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-02T03:09:13-07:00","id":1405904,"title":"","content":"Thanks, it\u2019s clear now.<br /> I missed the activation as part, so I was thinking Blink was a part of the defensive roll (and so a stunt you must buy using the roll).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-05T17:44:31-07:00","id":1406533,"title":"","content":"My group and I spent a couple of hours smashing our heads against the specifics of Auxiliary Modes, and I was hoping to get some clarification.<br /> <br /> On page 209 of the Trinity Continuum: Aeon rulebook it says - &quot;Auxiliary Modes also provide access to that Aptitude\u2019s basic powers. However, psions can\u2019t attempt to manifest greater effects than their Auxiliary Mode dots allow or combine Auxiliary Modes or their associated basic powers with any other powers, including their Aptitude.&quot;<br /> <br /> Firstly, what exactly does 'psions can't attempt to manifest greater effects than their Auxiliary Mode dots allow' mean? Is it:<br /> A) Psions with one dot in an Auxiliary Mode gain access to ONLY the Auxiliary Aptitude's Basic Powers AND ONLY the first (lowest) power in that specific mode.<br /> or<br /> B)Psions with one dot in an Auxiliary Mode gain access to the Auxiliary Aptitude's Basic Powers AND (whilst keeping within the rules that govern the use of powers beyond her mode dot) may attempt to use the higher powers in whichever Mode she's got the Auxiliary point in.<br /> or<br /> C) Something else completely...<br /> <br /> And secondly, what does '...(can't)...combine Auxiliary Modes or their basic associated powers with any other powers, including their Aptitude' mean, particularly in regards to Attunement? Does someone with an Auxiliary Mode dot in one of the Clairsentience disciplines need to choose between rolling more dice to Attune via their primary (due to the higher dice pool) and rolling fewer dice (albeit it with a chance of attaining the additional information and range that a Clear's 'The Sight' and 'Extended Attunement' provide), or is the act of Attuning an 'all of your Attunement abilities rolled into one' sort of thing?<br /> <br /> Thanks to all involved in the Trinity Continuum for their hard work and obvious enthusiasm. It absolutely shines through.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26350-hounded","name":"Hounded","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-06T02:50:18-07:00","id":1406602,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hounded</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1362003-ask-a-dev?p=1406533#post1406533\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A) Psions with one dot in an Auxiliary Mode gain access to ONLY the Auxiliary Aptitude's Basic Powers AND ONLY the first (lowest) power in that specific mode.</div> </div> </div> </div>A is the correct answer. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hounded</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1362003-ask-a-dev?p=1406533#post1406533\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Does someone with an Auxiliary Mode dot in one of the Clairsentience disciplines need to choose between rolling more dice to Attune via their primary (due to the higher dice pool) and rolling fewer dice (albeit it with a chance of attaining the additional information and range that a Clear's 'The Sight' and 'Extended Attunement' provide)</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes. Auxiliary Modes are a remnant that couldn\u2019t be entirely eliminated from psions, and don\u2019t function as smoothly as multiple Aptitudes would work for psiads.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-06T04:58:02-07:00","id":1406612,"title":"","content":"Awesome. Thank you so much for the clarification!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26350-hounded","name":"Hounded","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-06T06:21:23-07:00","id":1406621,"title":"","content":"Hello again!<br /> Three questions, this time regarding Storyguide Characters. <br /> <br /> On page 139 of the Core Rulebook, there is a nice table with the pools for these characters. But if I go to the Human Supporting Cast (AEON page 327), I notice that not only Major Characters do not correspond to these pools in the table, but that Minor Characters do not follow the rules at all, as they have Mental/Physical/Social pools and no Primary/Secondary/Desperation Pools.<br /> <br /> So, how are NPC managed?<br /> <br /> Also, another doubt I have is regarding modes. In order to keep a balance with the threat level they pose, they should be different if they are Minor/Medium/Moderate/Major/Colossal Threats (according to Core book). How many dots in modes should a Storyguide Character have?<br /> <br /> And last but not least... this threat level is according to what number of PC? Something that is lethal to two characters could be piece of cake to 7 characters...<br /> <br /> Thank you very much, again! :-)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26301-sothus","name":"Sothus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26301_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":1,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"15"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-06T14:39:41-07:00","id":1406674,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sothus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1362003-ask-a-dev?p=1406621#post1406621\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On page 139 of the Core Rulebook, there is a nice table with the pools for these characters. But if I go to the Human Supporting Cast (AEON page 327), I notice that not only Major Characters do not correspond to these pools in the table, but that Minor Characters do not follow the rules at all, as they have Mental/Physical/Social pools and no Primary/Secondary/Desperation Pools.</div> </div> </div> </div>The numbers and Attributes for Storyguide Characters in Trinity Continuum Core were revised and updated late in the production cycle, and unfortunately the numbers in TC: Aeon weren\u2019t adjusted to match before printing. Use the details in TC Core as the better calibrated numbers.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sothus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1362003-ask-a-dev?p=1406621#post1406621\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Also, another doubt I have is regarding modes. In order to keep a balance with the threat level they pose, they should be different if they are Minor/Medium/Moderate/Major/Colossal Threats (according to Core book). How many dots in modes should a Storyguide Character have?</div> </div> </div> </div>Use the Source and Anomaly Powers columns in the antagonist table (p.139) as a guide to how many total dots they may have.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sothus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1362003-ask-a-dev?p=1406621#post1406621\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> And last but not least... this threat level is according to what number of PC? Something that is lethal to two characters could be piece of cake to 7 characters...</div> </div> </div> </div>You\u2019ll have to figure out this one based on your group of characters, Their abilities, and the needs of your story.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-06T21:06:42-07:00","id":1406723,"title":"","content":"Is there official word yet on what has happened to specific American cities in the Aeon timeframe? Los Angeles, Chicago, or New York especially. Anything in any of the sourcebooks?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26346-fromage","name":"Fromage","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-06T21:21:18-07:00","id":1406724,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fromage</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1362003-ask-a-dev?p=1406723#post1406723\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is there official word yet on what has happened to specific American cities in the Aeon timeframe? Los Angeles, Chicago, or New York especially. Anything in any of the sourcebooks?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Further details on Earth will be in Terra Firma.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#800000\">Ian A. A. Watson</span></b><span style=\"color:#bdc3c7\">(he/she)</span><br /> <b>Onyx Path Community Manager<br /> Trinity Continuum Content Lead</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4-ianwatson","name":"IanWatson","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4_2.png","title":"Community Manager","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1512"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-09T11:18:22-07:00","id":1407160,"title":"","content":"Can Telekinesis be used to grapple someone? Lift them off the ground to keep them from being able to move around, etc? Most of the powers describe moving &quot;objects&quot; but it doesn't seem clear whether living beings are included in that category. Is there a standard system for resolving such attempts? How many dots would be necessary?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24779-shisumo","name":"Shisumo","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-09T14:31:03-07:00","id":1407185,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shisumo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1362003-ask-a-dev?p=1407160#post1407160\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can Telekinesis be used to grapple someone?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes. TK 2, Remote Hands. Note that it uses Psi instead of Might so adjust in the Grapple rules as well.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shisumo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1362003-ask-a-dev?p=1407160#post1407160\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Lift them off the ground to keep them from being able to move around, etc?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes. TK 4, Kinetic Enhancement, refer the second paragraph of the system.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-19T12:26:51-07:00","id":1409189,"title":"","content":"Here goes:<br /> Shameless Lying Smile the Talent Gift on page 214 in the Core Book... how does it work exactly?<br /> The description is easy enough, but the potential implications are another thing.<br /> <br /> So, here's the rub:<br /> How far goes that talent?<br /> Can a Talent put suggestions into people that are potentially far reaching and life altering or not?<br /> Can he spin stupid stuff like &quot;you drank truth serum and have to answer honest to god&quot;?<br /> <br /> I mean, could be pretty useful in the hands of a creative player, while in the hands of another it's just adding dice and complications.<br /> If for instance are suggestions are a possibility there is the option to turn a person into a manchurian candidate or a sleeper agent.<br /> Sure that would take a bit of time and cost Inspiration, but that's hardly a barrier.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9298-bhurano","name":"Bhurano","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"21"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-22T01:03:00-07:00","id":1409710,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bhurano</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1362003-ask-a-dev?p=1409189#post1409189\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Here goes:<br /> Shameless Lying Smile the Talent Gift on page 214 in the Core Book... how does it work exactly?<br /> The description is easy enough, but the potential implications are another thing.<br /> <br /> So, here's the rub:<br /> How far goes that talent?<br /> Can a Talent put suggestions into people that are potentially far reaching and life altering or not?<br /> Can he spin stupid stuff like &quot;you drank truth serum and have to answer honest to god&quot;?<br /> <br /> I mean, could be pretty useful in the hands of a creative player, while in the hands of another it's just adding dice and complications.<br /> If for instance are suggestions are a possibility there is the option to turn a person into a manchurian candidate or a sleeper agent.<br /> Sure that would take a bit of time and cost Inspiration, but that's hardly a barrier.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's lying, not mind control. Even in the hands of a creative player, it's still just dice and Complications. Having a bonus to lie doesn't mean the huge lies don't have their own Difficulties and Complications to overcome.<br /> <br /> The Talent with this can lie through their teeth and seem 100% convincing, but that doesn't make it true. And the more easily disprovable the lie, the harder it's going to be for the Talent to sustain. Even if a target is completely convinced they're still going to react in their own ways that might not be precisely what the Talent intends. And the final limitation - it lasts for a scene, after which the target might still believe the lies but they're more easily disprovable.<br /> <br /> Also, lying usually comes under the Influence systems, which specifically allow the victim to reject the Influence if they want. This will give the Talent Consolation, but it's not going to make automatic sleeper agents. <br /> <br /> Basically, if the Talent's lies are fun and advance the game, regardless of how influential they are, go with it. If they're too far, they won't work.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-23T07:05:49-07:00","id":1409891,"title":"","content":"In page3 104 of the Core Rulebook ,under Establish Grapple, it states that the successes needed are variable.<br /> Under the Grappled rules on the same page, it is stated that breaking/reversing a grapple is a contested Athletics+Attribute.<br /> <br /> But I cannot find the successes needed to establish the grapple...<br /> <br /> Thanks!<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26301-sothus","name":"Sothus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26301_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":1,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"15"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-23T08:12:40-07:00","id":1409911,"title":"","content":"Hello again... :-)<br /> A question regarding indirect damage (pag. 108.109 Core). On page 109 it is stated that by rolling Stamina+Resolve, a character can reduce the Injury Conditions taken by the source of damage. But what is the difficulty of the roll? The Damage Rating itself?<br /> <br /> Thanks again!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26301-sothus","name":"Sothus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26301_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":1,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"15"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-23T11:46:47-07:00","id":1409940,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bunyip</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1362003-ask-a-dev?p=1409710#post1409710\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It's lying, not mind control. Even in the hands of a creative player, it's still just dice and Complications. Having a bonus to lie doesn't mean the huge lies don't have their own Difficulties and Complications to overcome.<br /> <br /> The Talent with this can lie through their teeth and seem 100% convincing, but that doesn't make it true. And the more easily disprovable the lie, the harder it's going to be for the Talent to sustain. Even if a target is completely convinced they're still going to react in their own ways that might not be precisely what the Talent intends. And the final limitation - it lasts for a scene, after which the target might still believe the lies but they're more easily disprovable.<br /> <br /> Also, lying usually comes under the Influence systems, which specifically allow the victim to reject the Influence if they want. This will give the Talent Consolation, but it's not going to make automatic sleeper agents.<br /> <br /> Basically, if the Talent's lies are fun and advance the game, regardless of how influential they are, go with it. If they're too far, they won't work.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thank you, much appreciated.<br /> Those clarifications are EXTREMELY helpful.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9298-bhurano","name":"Bhurano","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"21"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-23T17:28:12-07:00","id":1409982,"title":"","content":"Is it allowed to write Adventure! themed shortstories to put on storypath nexus?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12074-robert-d","name":"Robert D","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"434"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-23T17:43:40-07:00","id":1409986,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Robert D</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1362003-ask-a-dev?p=1409982#post1409982\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is it allowed to write Adventure! themed shortstories to put on storypath nexus?</div> </div> </div> </div>You can read the Storypath Nexus Community Content Guidelines here: <a href=\"https://support.drivethrurpg.com/hc/en-us/articles/360029073732-Storypath-Nexus-Community-Content-Program-Guidelines\" target=\"_blank\">https://support.drivethrurpg.com/hc/...ram-Guidelines</a><br /> <br /> Note that Adventure! is listed in the &quot;Unavailable Games&quot; section.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#800000\">Ian A. A. Watson</span></b><span style=\"color:#bdc3c7\">(he/she)</span><br /> <b>Onyx Path Community Manager<br /> Trinity Continuum Content Lead</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4-ianwatson","name":"IanWatson","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4_2.png","title":"Community Manager","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1512"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-23T18:05:17-07:00","id":1409989,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>IanWatson</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1362003-ask-a-dev?p=1409986#post1409986\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You can read the Storypath Nexus Community Content Guidelines here: <a href=\"https://support.drivethrurpg.com/hc/en-us/articles/360029073732-Storypath-Nexus-Community-Content-Program-Guidelines\" target=\"_blank\">https://support.drivethrurpg.com/hc/...ram-Guidelines</a><br /> <br /> Note that Adventure! is listed in the &quot;Unavailable Games&quot; section.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thank you Ian! will do!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12074-robert-d","name":"Robert D","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"434"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-28T16:39:15-07:00","id":1410902,"title":"","content":"On the off-chance that the Aberrant developers are still developing: <br /> <br /> I had a minor idea I wished to share, in the hopes it might be helpful in some way. My thought was this: Perhaps we could tweak/modify Dense Flesh so that every third dot, instead of another Health Level, gave it's user a level of Hard Armor: basically, it could negate the first complication due to physical injury during the combat at Dot 3, two Complications at Dot 6, and three at Dot 9. Then, you could remove that as an option from Durability, leaving it as Soft Armor to reskin as either hard to land a damaging blow on (the Tank Option) or connect it to Mega-Dexterity as the Speedster Option. This nicely separates the two of them, makes Dense Flesh a bit more robust, and makes Durability more flexible. <br /> <br /> On the subject of Durability, what separates it from Skin Armor, besides having to pay for Skin Armor which, IIRC, isn't on all the time. Has that been looked at during the revisions? <br /> <br /> Anyway, on the off-chance someone checks this out, hope everything is proceeding smoothly, and hope to hear from you soon.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2176-spectaculartentacular","name":"SpectacularTentacular","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2176_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"179"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-28T23:35:26-07:00","id":1410955,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SpectacularTentacular</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1362003-ask-a-dev?p=1410902#post1410902\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On the off-chance that the Aberrant developers are still developing:</div> </div> </div> </div>As per the Monday Meeting Notes, Aberrant is in layout. I doubt its developers are looking to change any systems - or anything - right now.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-30T10:23:05-07:00","id":1411091,"title":"","content":"Form Mastery lets you buy a form based on Chimera. Chimera lets you build a weapon whose enhancements are determined by the number of successes spent on it. Form Mastery costs 1 xp per 2 successes required. So, for the price of a path dot, you could build a form with a weapon with 35 enhancement plus at least 4 points of tags. That would make it one of the most powerful base scale weapons in existence. Should there be any kind of limit to the number of successes you buy with Form Mastery? (I was thinking a total number of successes equal to Psi+Mode.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8719-florin","name":"Florin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"940"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-10T12:19:01-07:00","id":1412875,"title":"","content":"More a potential errata question regarding the Aeon era world map:<br /> <br /> - The world map shows this huge chunk of quantum flux corruption in Argentina, yet the rest of the book refers specifically to the Venezuelan Plaguelands. Map error and the big red blotch should cover most of Venezuela except for the coastline?<br /> - Same question for La Blessure. The book advises the corrupt zone stretching from France to Belgium with some impact in the Netherlands. Map shows it in northwestern France instead of northeastern. I imagine the red blotch should be in the area of Paris stretching east? Would make sense as the wind at that latitude blows from west to east and would shower any debris breaking off the falling station in an easterly direction.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2462-karlb","name":"KarlB","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2462_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"90"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-10T13:35:33-07:00","id":1412888,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KarlB</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1362003-ask-a-dev?p=1412875#post1412875\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">More a potential errata question regarding the Aeon era world map:<br /> <br /> Map error</div> </div> </div> </div>Some areas were inadvertently left off the map, yes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#800000\">Ian A. A. Watson</span></b><span style=\"color:#bdc3c7\">(he/she)</span><br /> <b>Onyx Path Community Manager<br /> Trinity Continuum Content Lead</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4-ianwatson","name":"IanWatson","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4_2.png","title":"Community Manager","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1512"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-27T03:22:15-07:00","id":1415663,"title":"","content":"What mode or combination of modes would be used to create coherent sound- music, voices, or anything more than random noise?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26448-shalmaneser","name":"Shalmaneser","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"79"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-27T06:45:10-07:00","id":1415679,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shalmaneser</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1362003-ask-a-dev?p=1415663#post1415663\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What mode or combination of modes would be used to create coherent sound- music, voices, or anything more than random noise?</div> </div> </div> </div>A creative use of Telekinesis (3-5 dots) or Energetics (2 dots) would probably be the best choices. Although it\u2019s not a short-term answer, Prometheus Unbound (the psi order book) will include systems for generating creative uses of Aptitudes and Modes this way.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-03T20:16:53-07:00","id":1416672,"title":"","content":"Random question about Telepathy and things like mind control and the influence mechanic. If a psion character (pc or npc) was planning on some long term mental manipulations to make someone loyal and whatnot would it make sense to say give them Enhancement to their various Intrigue rolls based on their general Psychebending dots. I mean there isn't a direct power that says 'you make a person yours in such a way that nobody can tell the person was manipulated' and I figure this is exactly what Enhancements might apply. <br /> <br /> Another idea I could see is having them use the Rewrite power from Psychebending to give the character some sort of permanent status condition. I'm not sure what to call it, maybe Dominated or something. Though in this case I don't entirely know how to go about it. <br /> <br /> I know this isn't a 'nice' question but there are many characters in fiction and such that use such powers for such gain and so I wanted to see how it would be done via Storypath Trinity.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/661-lordheru","name":"LordHeru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar661_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-04T04:15:42-07:00","id":1416708,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LordHeru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1362003-ask-a-dev?p=1416672#post1416672\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Random question about Telepathy and things like mind control and the influence mechanic. If a psion character (pc or npc) was planning on some long term mental manipulations to make someone loyal and whatnot would it make sense to say give them Enhancement to their various Intrigue rolls based on their general Psychebending dots. I mean there isn't a direct power that says 'you make a person yours in such a way that nobody can tell the person was manipulated' and I figure this is exactly what Enhancements might apply. <br /> <br /> Another idea I could see is having them use the Rewrite power from Psychebending to give the character some sort of permanent status condition. I'm not sure what to call it, maybe Dominated or something. Though in this case I don't entirely know how to go about it. <br /> <br /> I know this isn't a 'nice' question but there are many characters in fiction and such that use such powers for such gain and so I wanted to see how it would be done via Storypath Trinity.</div> </div> </div> </div>It\u2019s certainly something you could try. The answer to this is much like my answer to the previous question, but may not be satisfying for people wanting things right now! Prometheus Unbound Will have psi systems that help with creative effects like these.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-04T06:57:43-07:00","id":1416719,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bunyip</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1362003-ask-a-dev?p=1416708#post1416708\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It\u2019s certainly something you could try. The answer to this is much like my answer to the previous question, but may not be satisfying for people wanting things right now! Prometheus Unbound Will have psi systems that help with creative effects like these.</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually this does help me. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> So thanks. <br /> <br /> Basucally, I didn't miss something as written. Also as this was a theoretical I can totally wait. <br /> <br /> So yeah this totally helps.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/661-lordheru","name":"LordHeru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar661_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-07T21:32:05-07:00","id":1417257,"title":"","content":"Random question that I had by going through the book due to my recent post - <br /> <br /> Could a psion use either Photonic Power or Dynamic Control to basically etch engravings on say a crystal. And if so could such engravings be read as information like say a CD. Furthermore, could a Electrokinetic work with a Clair with Psycholocation Focus Sensing be able to etch say microscopically or even smaller. <br /> <br /> Cause if so I am imagining a revolution in the digital storage medium used by certain elite groups.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/661-lordheru","name":"LordHeru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar661_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-10T03:59:50-07:00","id":1417530,"title":"","content":"How long would it take a psion character with psi 7 and vitakinesis to heal if all injury condition boxes are checked? If I'm reading this right, Knit would downgrade the psion's most severe injury condition each round, but with all boxes checked the psion has no box to &quot;downgrade&quot; the maimed condition to. Would they have to heal by other means until their Bruised and Injured conditions were gone, after which Maimed would heal itself in a couple of rounds?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26448-shalmaneser","name":"Shalmaneser","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"79"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-11T05:06:56-07:00","id":1417622,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shalmaneser</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1362003-ask-a-dev?p=1417530#post1417530\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How long would it take a psion character with psi 7 and vitakinesis to heal if all injury condition boxes are checked? If I'm reading this right, Knit would downgrade the psion's most severe injury condition each round, but with all boxes checked the psion has no box to &amp;quot;downgrade&amp;quot; the maimed condition to. Would they have to heal by other means until their Bruised and Injured conditions were gone, after which Maimed would heal itself in a couple of rounds?</div> </div> </div> </div>If all Injury Condition boxes are checked, the vitakinetic has nowhere to downgrade damage. Without removing the Bruised level they\u2019re stuck. Once Bruised is gone, either through Iatrosis or some other means, the Psi 7 proxy will be fine in a matter of moments.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-11T18:18:30-07:00","id":1417740,"title":"","content":"So you can't downgrade Bruised to &quot;nothing&quot;?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8719-florin","name":"Florin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"940"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-12T00:15:01-07:00","id":1417777,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Florin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1362003-ask-a-dev?p=1417740#post1417740\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So you can't downgrade Bruised to &amp;quot;nothing&amp;quot;?</div> </div> </div> </div>By a strict interpretation of the wording, no. However, the intent of the effect is that VKs keep healing unless dead, so I\u2019d let the Maimed downgrade to Injured, which pushes the Injured to Bruised, and eliminates the Bruised condition. But, Taken Out is still taken out - if you can hit a VK fast and hard enough, you take them out. They may start the next scene completely healed, but they don\u2019t get to keep acting in this scene.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-21T08:07:47-07:00","id":1419375,"title":"","content":"Im not getting something about Novas Elemental Mastery. The manuscript says<br /> &quot;Choose one of the following base effects for the nova\u2019s Elemental Mastery: Environmental Anima, Quantum Anima, Quantum Attack, or Shroud, all using the chosen element as the medium.&quot;<br /> <br /> But im not seeing anything in those powers that says that Elemental Mastery is a prerequisite. So can i take Quantum Attack alone to do generic ranged attacks?<br /> <br /> If its like that, what is the function of Elemental Mastery?<br /> <br /> Also, about the Agent power, how does that power works if i want several types of Agents. Like a horde of simple minions, a few stronger ones and a single big guy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1351,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1351-sakii","user":"Sakii","date":". 10-21-2020, 02:14 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1351-sakii","name":"Sakii","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1351_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-23T20:29:32-07:00","id":1419902,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MoroseMorgan</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> By the language of First Aid on Core on page 108,<br /> &amp;quot;The Bruised condition is removed when<br /> downgraded&amp;quot;<br /> So downgrading to nothing is a thing, and all is well.</div> </div> </div> </div>That\u2019s not the issue. The issue is that the Knit power specifically downgrades the highest level of damage. If you have Bruised and Injured already filled, Maimed has nowhere to go to downgrade. It\u2019s my fault with the wording, the intent is that you shuffle along all the Injury Conditions from the most serious.<br /> <br /> Some example scenarios with the intent. Say a character has the standard Bruised, Injured, and Maimed boxes available. Ignore how long the Specific healing time for this character is, I\u2019ll just say \u2018when they heal\u2019:<br /> <br /> 1 - The character marks off Bruised and nothing else. When they heal, they downgrade the Bruised and are fully healed.<br /> 2 - The character marks off Bruised and Injured. When they heal, they downgrade the Bruised and Injured, leaving just the Bruised. (Or, as it appears In practice, they just remove the Injured.)<br /> 3 - The character marks off Injured and Maimed. When they heal, they downgrade the Injured and Maimed, leaving Bruised and Injured.<br /> 4 - The character marks off Bruised, Injured, and Maimed. When they heal, they downgrade the Bruised, Injured, and Maimed, leaving the Bruised and Injured. (It appears that you just remove the Maimed.)<br /> <br /> (This is where it gets a little trickier.)<br /> 5 - The character marks off Bruised and Maimed. When they heal, the Maimed downgrades to Injured, leaving Bruised and Injured marked.<br /> 6 - The character marks off Injured. When they heal, they downgrade Injured to Bruised. When they heal again, they remove the Bruised.<br /> 7 - The character marks off Maimed. When they heal, they downgrade the Maimed to Injured. When they heal again, they downgrade Injured to Bruised, and when they heal again, they remove Bruised.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-24T15:54:53-07:00","id":1420036,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bunyip</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1362003-ask-a-dev?p=1419902#post1419902\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That\u2019s not the issue. The issue is that the Knit power specifically downgrades the highest level of damage. If you have Bruised and Injured already filled, Maimed has nowhere to go to downgrade. It\u2019s my fault with the wording, the intent is that you shuffle along all the Injury Conditions from the most serious.<br /> <br /> Some example scenarios with the intent. Say a character has the standard Bruised, Injured, and Maimed boxes available. Ignore how long the Specific healing time for this character is, I\u2019ll just say \u2018when they heal\u2019:<br /> <br /> 1 - The character marks off Bruised and nothing else. When they heal, they downgrade the Bruised and are fully healed.<br /> 2 - The character marks off Bruised and Injured. When they heal, they downgrade the Bruised and Injured, leaving just the Bruised. (Or, as it appears In practice, they just remove the Injured.)<br /> 3 - The character marks off Injured and Maimed. When they heal, they downgrade the Injured and Maimed, leaving Bruised and Injured.<br /> 4 - The character marks off Bruised, Injured, and Maimed. When they heal, they downgrade the Bruised, Injured, and Maimed, leaving the Bruised and Injured. (It appears that you just remove the Maimed.)<br /> <br /> (This is where it gets a little trickier.)<br /> 5 - The character marks off Bruised and Maimed. When they heal, the Maimed downgrades to Injured, leaving Bruised and Injured marked.<br /> 6 - The character marks off Injured. When they heal, they downgrade Injured to Bruised. When they heal again, they remove the Bruised.<br /> 7 - The character marks off Maimed. When they heal, they downgrade the Maimed to Injured. When they heal again, they downgrade Injured to Bruised, and when they heal again, they remove Bruised.</div> </div> </div> </div>I reread your original post shortly after posting mine and realized I was a bit off on what the issue was.<br /> <br /> I thought it was about how if you are full up you can't &quot;downgrade the highest&quot; from knit, but I hadn't considered it moves everything down the line at once like in Number 4. I thought you would need First Aid to clear up your Bruised so the train could move along.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Raksha are my fae-vorite.<br /> <br /> Reincarnation of magnificentmomo.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1542-morosemorgan","name":"MoroseMorgan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1542_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"778"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-24T18:23:04-07:00","id":1420055,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MoroseMorgan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1362003-ask-a-dev?p=1420036#post1420036\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I thought it was about how if you are full up you can't &amp;quot;downgrade the highest&amp;quot; from knit, but I hadn't considered it moves everything down the line at once like in Number 4. I thought you would need First Aid to clear up your Bruised so the train could move along.</div> </div> </div> </div>That is the problem and the RAW solution. But it\u2019s not quite RAI, as vitakinetics should be constantly healing themselves without having to wait for mundane first aid.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-26T19:18:15-07:00","id":1420384,"title":"","content":"Is there an errata page or pdf to clear up some of the confusion with rules interpretation?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2421-cknight","name":"cKnight","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"47"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-27T03:20:01-07:00","id":1420424,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>cKnight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1362003-ask-a-dev?p=1420384#post1420384\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is there an errata page or pdf to clear up some of the confusion with rules interpretation?</div> </div> </div> </div>Not as yet, no. Some fan made ones exist.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-27T07:20:30-07:00","id":1420467,"title":"","content":"Could not find this asked before, so here it is:<br /> <br /> How does Dynamic Control work, in practice?<br /> <br /> What I get is this:<br /> <br /> You roll dynamically for it to be activated, then assign the uses for Mode electromagnetic broadcasts. <br /> <br /> &quot;Once activated, each laser or other beam functions on its own, but moving, altering, or redirecting more than one of these lasers per round requires a mixed action.&quot;<br /> <br /> What about the next turns, if you do not reassign anything, how many successes does it get on the attack? Do you roll for each attack separately and reflexively (with a full pool)? Or do you roll reflexively psi + mode + enhancements and assign successes for each task (defend, attack, wall, rework data) in a mixed roll? Or is the mixed roll to define successes for attacking, defending, etc, not reflexive? Or is it only non-reflexive when you reassign operations?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1524-pcontop","name":"pcontop","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1524_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"278"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-28T04:47:42-07:00","id":1420654,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>pcontop</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1362003-ask-a-dev?p=1420467#post1420467\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Could not find this asked before, so here it is:<br /> <br /> How does Dynamic Control work, in practice?</div> </div> </div> </div>Just noting that I\u2019ve seen this and will get back to you soon, but can\u2019t today.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-30T12:43:49-07:00","id":1421036,"title":"","content":"Looking through the Aberrant backer PDF, very excited!<br /> <br /> I like the new implementation of Techniques using a mega-edge.<br /> <br /> Question on Power Suites and mixed actions.<br /> <br /> Say I have a Power Suite that is Elemental Mastery Fire, with the sub-powers Quantum Attack (Beam) [a flamethrower like attack] and Flight [rocket flames from my feat].<br /> Using my quantum attack while flying is a Mixed Action, and therefore I cannot use the Spray stunt?<br /> <br /> How would this be different if I had Flight and Quantum Attack as independent powers not part of a Suite (aside from costing more XP wise)? <br /> <br /> Essentially, could you give me a few specific examples of setups where a power suite is WORSE than having the powers separately aside from the XP cost/savings?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/509-tiwaztyrsfist","name":"TiwazTyrsfist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar509_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"162"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-30T17:41:50-07:00","id":1421073,"title":"","content":"With the Technique mega-edge, if I increase the xp cost on the base power, do the other powers in the suite change at all?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8719-florin","name":"Florin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"940"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-30T23:22:12-07:00","id":1421123,"title":"","content":"Is there any amount of pointing out what \u201cBender\u201d means in the U.K. that will get you guys to rethink Corbin\u2019s moniker? His writeup references a \u201cdouble-meaning\u201d with regard to his drinking, but does not acknowledge he\u2019s walking around calling himself a pejorative for gay men.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-30T23:55:43-07:00","id":1421127,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1362003-ask-a-dev?p=1421123#post1421123\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is there any amount of pointing out what \u201cBender\u201d means in the U.K. that will get you guys to rethink Corbin\u2019s moniker?</div> </div> </div> </div>We had extensive conversations about it and ultimately decided to leave it as is. Aberrant errata, however, is not what the Ask A Dev thread is for. You're welcome to use the errata form if you disagree with our decison.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#800000\">Ian A. A. Watson</span></b><span style=\"color:#bdc3c7\">(he/she)</span><br /> <b>Onyx Path Community Manager<br /> Trinity Continuum Content Lead</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4-ianwatson","name":"IanWatson","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4_2.png","title":"Community Manager","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1512"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-31T04:28:41-07:00","id":1421143,"title":"","content":"Alright, with the backer PDF out, I'm checking out various revisions compared to the preview, and I hit a minor snag in chargen. I see the new option for taking Transformations to discount things replacing the &quot;take a point of Transcendence for half cost&quot; option, but that option still appears on page 90. I just want to make sure that either both options exist, or if one supersedes the other.<br /> <br /> On that note, the 'take a Transformation for an XP discount' option only lists low and mid level transformations. Are high level ones intended to be impossible at chargen, and if one wished to allow it anyway what would an appropriate discount be?<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2334-aliasi","name":"Aliasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2334_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"197"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-31T08:47:33-07:00","id":1421165,"title":"","content":"Forgot this was the Ask the Dev thread","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8719-florin","name":"Florin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"940"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-31T10:11:26-07:00","id":1421172,"title":"","content":"Q-Tech questions:<br /> 1. Buying Qtech item requires the Q-Tech experience cost listed in page 94 or do you need to build it as in the rules of q-tech construction?<br /> 2. I believe Qtech construction referencing Q-Tech Mega Edge is referring to this Experience cost, not to the Mega Edge itself. Is that right?<br /> 3. Can you attune to a device (maybe temporarily) without paying the experience cost?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-01T02:30:10-08:00","id":1421273,"title":"","content":"Aberrant Preview Question here: I noticed that the Mega-Edges MENTAL FOCUS and QUANTUM STABILITY appear to have vanished. Mental Focus seems to be particularly missed, since there seems to be no other way to combat mental powers, unless the Scale bonus from Mega-Composure plays a part.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2176-spectaculartentacular","name":"SpectacularTentacular","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2176_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"179"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-01T18:57:30-08:00","id":1421377,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SpectacularTentacular</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1362003-ask-a-dev?p=1421273#post1421273\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Aberrant Preview Question here: I noticed that the Mega-Edges MENTAL FOCUS and QUANTUM STABILITY appear to have vanished. Mental Focus seems to be particularly missed, since there seems to be no other way to combat mental powers, unless the Scale bonus from Mega-Composure plays a part.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Is Mega-Composure meant to grant Scale? (yes this is a dev question, but it's a follow up inspired by the above)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-01T19:02:58-08:00","id":1421378,"title":"","content":"Is Leadership Scale supposed to grant stronger social power over individuals, or does it just increase the number of people that can be influenced at once without penalty?<br /> <br /> - if the latter, how does it interact with Mass Influence doing the same thing?<br /> <br /> - If the former does that mean if a Mega-Presence 6 Nova tries to command the President of the US (Leadership Scale 7 by the Chart on 164), it's an unmodified roll, and any Nova with lower Mega-Presence would be operating at a Scale deficit?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-03T20:00:56-08:00","id":1421726,"title":"","content":"Is taking a transformation to reduce the exp cost for a nova trait permanent or only for a single purchase?<br /> <br /> With the Quantum Agent power and the tag Horde i can create an army of creatures, but im not finding some kind of mass combat rules.<br /> How do i rule a fight of 1000 vs 1?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1351,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1351-sakii","user":"Sakii","date":". 11-03-2020, 11:24 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1351-sakii","name":"Sakii","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1351_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-05T05:58:48-08:00","id":1421990,"title":"","content":"Hey, overall rules are great, just have a few quick questions. I'm mostly trying to make sure certain things are design decisions and not errors, and also figure out the reasoning behind them to see if I'm missing something.<br /> <br /> 1) It is deliberate that Mega-Might and Toughness be one Scale better than Quantum Attack and Quantum Field? If so, why? Are there tradeoffs that make the latter two better in other ways?<br /> <br /> 2) Is Quantum Deflection really not supposed to grant Scale? It seems really weak right now.<br /> <br /> With Quantum 5 and Quantum Deflection 5, it basically gives Defense +4 against a single attack or less against multiple attacks, and costs 2 points per round. Whereas at that level, Quantum Field would give the equivalent of about Defense +10 that works against every attack and only cost 1 point per scene, and Toughness would give Defense +12 against every attack and not cost anything. Is there something about Quantum Deflection that makes it better than I'm thinking?<br /> <br /> 3) How strong are the quick NPC novas from the antagonists chapter supposed to be compared to the average PC? Are they supposed to be serious threats or more like lackeys? They seem to be a bit on the weak side.<br /> <br /> 4) I realize that Aeon and Aberrant have different rules, even though they seem similar, and you can't really assume that something in one works the same way in the other. But in setting terms, are the sample crazed space monster aberrants from Aeon supposed to be stronger than modern novas, equivalent to them, or weaker than them?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1711-zeea","name":"Zeea","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"106"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-06T16:12:08-08:00","id":1422322,"title":"","content":"Also, is Attunement gone? Has it been folded into the rules somewhere and I'm just missing it?<br /> <br /> EDIT: Never mind! I fail at reading stuff.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2176,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2176-spectaculartentacular","user":"SpectacularTentacular","date":". 11-12-2020, 05:10 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2176-spectaculartentacular","name":"SpectacularTentacular","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2176_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"179"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-07T16:44:43-08:00","id":1422512,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mateus Luz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1362003-ask-a-dev?p=1421172#post1421172\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Q-Tech questions:<br /> 1. Buying Qtech item requires the Q-Tech experience cost listed in page 94 or do you need to build it as in the rules of q-tech construction?<br /> 2. I believe Qtech construction referencing Q-Tech Mega Edge is referring to this Experience cost, not to the Mega Edge itself. Is that right?<br /> 3. Can you attune to a device (maybe temporarily) without paying the experience cost?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Seconding this. The wording and the way things are spread out makes it hard to understand how this is supposed to work. The cost for starting with a Q-tech item is also really unclear.<ul><li>Do I need to purchase the Artifact Edge, and then the Attunement Edge?</li> <li>If I want to start with two Q-tech items do I purchase Artifact twice, Attunement, and then the Q-Tech Medge-Edge?</li> <li>Do I need to pay 12xps per rank of the Q-tech Device to attune it on top of those costs?</li> </ul>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4270-literatzi","name":"literatzi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4270_2.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-09T03:27:04-08:00","id":1422716,"title":"","content":"Thirding this. The Q-Tech rules don't make a lot of sense and openly contradict each other in places, and the quick character templates seem to be using completely different rules.<br /> <br /> Page 233 says you can't use Artifact to acquire Q-Tech devices. It does say novas can attune one piece of Q-Tech, and Attunement and Q-Tech edges can allow for more. But there's no rules for _owning_ Q-Tech, just how much you could attune if you did get them. Are we supposed to assume a nova can start with as many ranks of Q-Tech devices as they can attune?<br /> <br /> Let's say I want a character to start with a blaster than works like Quantum Attack 2, a force field that works like Quantum Field 2, and a flying device that works like Flight 2. How would I make that character, how much does it cost to equip/attune all three of those devices, how much Quantum do I have to pay to fire the blaster each time, and how much Quantum do I have to pay to turn on the Quantum Field or Flight?<br /> <br /> EDIT: On page 237 it says &quot;the player must spend Experiences to purchase the item as the Q-Tech Mega-Edge.&quot; But that's not how the Q-Tech Mega-Edge is written as working.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1711,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1711-zeea","user":"Zeea","date":". 11-09-2020, 06:35 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1711-zeea","name":"Zeea","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"106"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-10T11:36:00-08:00","id":1422929,"title":"","content":"I am a bit curious how the variable power tag works. Am I thinking about this right? Say you want a quantum attack that can be used in close combat and also has the following tags, range 3 (variable 3) [so you can turn the range on and off], area 2 (variable 2) [so you can turn the blast on and off]<br /> <br /> Is that right or do you have to buy variable for each possible combination effectively making mini power suites? This is rather confusing to me. If it is the case that Variable is just the Technique mega edge but confined to the same power that also makes it quite easy.<br /> <br /> I know that this would be very expensive with all the power tags, but it is worth it for the example.<br /> <br /> Also, how does the variable tag interact with the negative power tags? What if I wanted to have a power that was always restricted, but the restriction was variable for instance?<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24929-econclark","name":"econclark","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-10T12:12:40-08:00","id":1422934,"title":"","content":"Not a mod or a dev, so my apologies if I'm stepping on toes, but only devs are allowed to answer questions in this thread, and they apparently are not answering any Aberrant questions right now (probably due to being in the middle of the errata phase.) If anyone actually wants an answer right now, you should probably post a new thread or in one of the other Aberrant threads where people are discussing how things work in the backer PDF.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8719-florin","name":"Florin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"940"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-10T15:16:55-08:00","id":1422970,"title":"","content":"Just to be clear to the devs here, my posts aren't exactly urgent questions or anything. It'd be nice to get a dev answer, but I'm not expecting or demanding one and especially not expecting one any time soon with everything going on with work and world events in general.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1711-zeea","name":"Zeea","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"106"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-10T15:27:57-08:00","id":1422974,"title":"","content":"Hey all! If the Q-Tech, variable tags, or other Aberrant stuff is confusing, it would be great if specific concerns were put into the errata form, so we can have everything in one place and look to see if anything needs clarifying. Once the rulebook is finalized, then we can answer lingering questions here, but yeah, our focus right now is on the errata. Thanks!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/15-eddyfate","name":"eddyfate","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar15_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"155"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-10T15:44:18-08:00","id":1422978,"title":"","content":"If you need the errata form link, here it is! <a href=\"https://forms.gle/CkJ5GXjny32nPauW7\" target=\"_blank\">https://forms.gle/CkJ5GXjny32nPauW7</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/15-eddyfate","name":"eddyfate","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar15_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"155"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-13T17:21:41-08:00","id":1423652,"title":"","content":"We've just started playing, so apologies if this is an obvious question, but we're wondering how Small Unit Tactics works - does the character need to take an action to give an ally the +2 enhancement, or do they just give it to someone every turn. Or is there some other mechanic for how it works that I've not found?<br /> <br /> Thanks","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26534-malladin-ben","name":"malladin.ben","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-16T10:42:04-08:00","id":1424306,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>malladin.ben</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1362003-ask-a-dev?p=1423652#post1423652\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">We've just started playing, so apologies if this is an obvious question, but we're wondering how Small Unit Tactics works - does the character need to take an action to give an ally the +2 enhancement, or do they just give it to someone every turn. Or is there some other mechanic for how it works that I've not found?<br /> <br /> Thanks</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah, a good question. I'll admit there are a few Edges that aren't worded exactly as I'd want them to be to be as playable as possible. It's supposed to be that whomever has the Edge can gain a +2 Enhancement to a combat action they are taking if they are doing it as part of a group effort. So say that if everyone in the team is concentrating fire on a single enemy, then the Edge user will get this +2 Enhancement to their attack. But if that person was attacking a target solo, then the Enhancement won't apply.<br /> <br /> I hope that clarifies it for you!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Danielle Lauzon, Requiem Developer, Storypath Guru, freelance writer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6155-impernious","name":"impernious","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"37"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-16T11:25:30-08:00","id":1424314,"title":"","content":"Re: Aberrant Q-tech devices. Please please please submit errata before the form closes tomorrow, including any confusion you notice from technology.<br /> <br /> In short, you need to have the Attunement Edge to have a single Q-tech device attuned to your character. If you have the Q-tech mega-edge it adds the number of devices you can have attuned (and seems to replace the attunement edge for determining what rank and how many right now, which I might make a note to change so that you can always have your attuned device from that). <br /> <br /> So, if you want to start a character with a single piece of Q-tech and don't plan on getting more, you can purchase the Attunement Edge (for relatively cheap, IMO) and get a piece of up to rank 5 (depending on how many dots you spend in attune). But if you want 3 different pieces, you'll want Q-tech mega-edge. So in the example Zeea gave of 3 different rank 3 devices (2 dots of Quantum powers puts those devices at Rank 3) means the character will need 9 dots worth of attunement from the Q-tech and Attunement Edges. So the first device needs the Attunement Edge at 3 dots, then you'll want the Q-tech Edge to get the ability to attune additional items to get the next 6 Ranks worth of Q-tech. So if the character has Quantum 3, they'll need the Q-tech Mega-Edge at 3. <br /> <br /> Please make a note in the errata form for me so I don't forget. The Q-tech mega-edge should also have language to include the q-tech device you can attune with the Attunement Edge.<br /> <br /> Note that you don't use wealth to gain Q-tech because it is uniquely made by novas for novas. This isn't something you can purchase with money, only make. But certainly if you've spent the experience points for the Edges to have items, then that is where you are spending your xp rather than buying the quantum powers themselves, so you should absolutely be able to start with devices on the character sheet rather than having to make them in game. When you get (or make) a new Q-tech device, if you don't have enough edge-dots worth of space for attunement, then you'll need to purchase more dots in the Q-tech Mega-Edge to accommodate it. But the language on p. 237 can also stand to be cleaned up a little bit to reflect that.<br /> <br /> As for how much Quantum - right now you spend 2 that you don't get back per rank of q-tech you have attuned. Then you spend the normal Quantum activation cost to use the item. If you feel like that's too costly, please submit a comment in the errata and we'll consider tuning it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Danielle Lauzon, Requiem Developer, Storypath Guru, freelance writer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6155-impernious","name":"impernious","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"37"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-16T12:58:17-08:00","id":1424335,"title":"","content":"Thanks Danielle!<br /> <br /> This made me rethink the way Super tech is gained by both Talents and Psions too. It made more clear what I was suspecting, Super tech is equipment, and so don\u2019t cost XP, unless you take it too far from your pay check (2 x Wealth + Source).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-16T13:57:41-08:00","id":1424343,"title":"","content":"Thanks so much, impernious. That clears up a LOT for me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1711-zeea","name":"Zeea","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"106"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-16T14:39:34-08:00","id":1424355,"title":"","content":"Also, for crafting, There are some things that I still don't quite understand. What is the trade-off between Maximum Enhancement and Maximum Edge Dot? How do you add Tag bonuses? When do you have to take it up to the next Rank? Do Nova Specific Edges count as Inspired Edges?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24929-econclark","name":"econclark","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-17T07:08:35-08:00","id":1424535,"title":"","content":"for the modules, am I missing something or is it possible to just make a Mega Edge Module with as many dots in Technique as you can handle, and construct a power suite this way? Also since it is a module, you can construct other settings etc for it that you could possibly swap as quickly as an ordinary action? That part actually seems really cool if it is possible. not sure if that belongs in the errata. <br /> <br /> Also, When you get Q-tech if it has quantum abilities, how do you determine how much space is left for edges/enhancements etc... before increasing the rank? <br /> <br /> I like that there is a conversion for shifting the paradigm but that seems too restrictive to apply everywhere.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24929-econclark","name":"econclark","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-20T12:53:22-08:00","id":1425229,"title":"","content":"I have a couple of questions about the stunts in the Aeon book (pg 275) -<br /> <br /> Are these stunts melee or ranged or both?<br /> How long does the defence penalty for Hobble last?<br /> <br /> thanks","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26534,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26534-malladin-ben","user":"malladin.ben","date":". 11-21-2020, 02:32 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26534-malladin-ben","name":"malladin.ben","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-22T07:28:32-08:00","id":1425512,"title":"","content":"Sorry, I have another rules query. How does Blink work?<br /> <br /> ... normally, if a character is attacked they roll Resolve, Stamina or Composure and successes generated are spent on stunts. One of which is dodge which adds successes spent to defence, which is the difficulty needed to hit them with the attack.<br /> <br /> With Blink a teleporter adds a new defensive stunt, so do they buy this with their resolve/stamina/composure roll successes which then let's them make a Psi+Translation roll to determine the effect of the outcome? If so what is the cost of this stunt? 0?<br /> <br /> Does the teleporter have to take an action to activate blink, and that action makes the defensive stunt available to them? If so, for how long and what is the stunt cost?<br /> <br /> Or does the teleporter have to use their action to use blink that turn, a little like a total defence action but using psi+translocation instead?<br /> <br /> Or something else entirely?<br /> <br /> Thanks","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26534-malladin-ben","name":"malladin.ben","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-21T05:18:52-08:00","id":1429333,"title":"","content":"So I ran into an odd situation with an aberrant game I'm running. I have two PC's, one with a Destructive Tag Quantum Attack, power scale 2, and another with Mega-Might 2, power scale 3. Just going to call them &quot;Blast&quot; and &quot;Muscles&quot; respectively in hopes this example doesn't get confusing. Blast's destructive tag lowers the NPC's defense of 3 to 1, and with a higher power scale can purchase &quot;Inflict Injury&quot; a second time. Inflict Injury normally costs the target's soft armor rating, but for NPC's that's just rolled into their defense. So defense 1, pays one success for the original Inflict, another 1 success for the second Inflict. <br /> <br /> Muscles punches an NPC with the same stats. He's got nothing that inherently lowers the targets defense, so he buys his first Inflict Injury for 3 successes. He'd normally pay the Soft Armor rating for the second and third Inflicts, but with soft armor rolled into defense I just sort of assumed the cost of those would be 3 as well.<br /> <br /> Questions,<br /> 1. Is this correct, or If the NPC has no separate soft armor rating should it be zero for the additional purchases of Inflict? <br /> <br /> 2. If it's zero, and NPC's don't have a separate soft armor rating, how do you make a challenging sort of BBEG that doesn't just get splatted unless you stat out his defense and soft armor?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26605-corbin_amsel","name":"corbin_amsel","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-25T00:00:27-08:00","id":1429832,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>malladin.ben</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1362003-ask-a-dev?p=1425512#post1425512\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sorry, I have another rules query. How does Blink work?</div> </div> </div> </div>Okay, it\u2019s a Psi Power, so the first thing is you have to activate it. Ordinary Action, Psi + Mode Dots as your dice pool. Once activated, it persists Mode Dots x Duration unless you commit a Psi point to maintain it. (The duration got left out of the description, sorry.) Pay attention to your successes, you\u2019ll need those for the defensive stunt. If you don\u2019t activate it, the Teleporter can\u2019t access the additional stunt.<br /> <br /> When Blink is active the character has an additional defensive option available. Instead of Dodge, Dive to Cover, or Roll Away, they can choose Blink. Blink works like a combination of Dodge and Roll Away. When attacked and the character uses Blink, she adds the successes from the Psi Activation roll to to her Defense and also teleports up to one range band away from the attacker.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-25T08:22:31-08:00","id":1429863,"title":"","content":"Any chance of getting Official character sheets for Psiads and/or Superiors in the near future? I'd really like some for my group. Kit-bashing only goes so far.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2318-johntfs","name":"johntfs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"373"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-25T10:36:01-08:00","id":1429875,"title":"","content":"Do drawback penalties stack with each other? Like, would the -1 penalty to social interactions from the Mars Adaptation and the -2 penalty from the Photosynthetic Edge result in a -3 penalty for a character with those 2 Edges?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>When will you rage?","edited":{"userid":1405,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1405-anteros","user":"Anteros","date":". 12-25-2020, 03:50 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1405-anteros","name":"Anteros","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1405_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"661"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-28T05:10:20-08:00","id":1430213,"title":"","content":"1) Does Max Mercer have time manipulation powers? (if I remember correctly, he had them in 1st edition)<br /> 2) Can he travel to any &quot;timepoint&quot; he wants? If not, what are his limitations/how his powers work?<br /> 3) Can he travel to the &quot;other Earths&quot; that form the Trinity Continuum multiverse?<br /> 4) What else can he do (time-related or not)?<br /> 5) What are the &quot;time travel laws&quot; of Trinity Continuum? I mean, does the Continuum work like &quot;Dark (TV series)&quot; or &quot;C\u00b0ntinuum: Roleplaying in the Yet&quot; -- or is it more like Back to the Future or another fiction work? (please cite the one that more closely resemble your vision of time travel for Trinity Continuum)<br /> 6) Do you intend to use Time Travel as a mechanic for NPCs or PCs in any Trinity Continuum upcoming book?<br /> <br /> Thank you! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1001-timecrafter","name":"Timecrafter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1001_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"134"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-28T05:22:38-08:00","id":1430216,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Timecrafter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1362003-ask-a-dev?p=1430213#post1430213\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1) Does Max Mercer have time manipulation powers? (if I remember correctly, he had them in 1st edition)</div> </div> </div> </div>Mercer's capabilities are covered on \u00c6on p. 257, and Aberrant p. 276, both in their respective Setting Secrets chapters.<br /> <br /> Most of the rest of your questions do not yet have canonical answers, so you'll have to wait and see.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 5) What are the &quot;time travel laws&quot; of Trinity Continuum? I mean, does the Continuum work like &quot;Dark (TV series)&quot; or &quot;C\u00b0ntinuum: Roleplaying in the Yet&quot; -- or is it more like Back to the Future or another fiction work? (please cite the one that more closely resemble your vision of time travel for Trinity Continuum) </div> </div> </div>Generally speaking, time travel works similarly to the way it's described in Avengers: Endgame.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 6) Do you intend to use Time Travel as a mechanic for NPCs or PCs in any Trinity Continuum upcoming book? </div> </div> </div>Hopefully.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#800000\">Ian A. A. Watson</span></b><span style=\"color:#bdc3c7\">(he/she)</span><br /> <b>Onyx Path Community Manager<br /> Trinity Continuum Content Lead</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4-ianwatson","name":"IanWatson","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4_2.png","title":"Community Manager","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1512"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-28T18:43:19-08:00","id":1430292,"title":"","content":"So....do you have broad plans for high-Quantum powers like in 1E? Or is it just the core game powers with lots of Tags?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2176-spectaculartentacular","name":"SpectacularTentacular","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2176_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"179"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-28T19:30:15-08:00","id":1430295,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SpectacularTentacular</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1362003-ask-a-dev?p=1430292#post1430292\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So....do you have broad plans for high-Quantum powers like in 1E? Or is it just the core game powers with lots of Tags?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> We have no plans for quantum powers beyond what's in Aberrant.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#800000\">Ian A. A. Watson</span></b><span style=\"color:#bdc3c7\">(he/she)</span><br /> <b>Onyx Path Community Manager<br /> Trinity Continuum Content Lead</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4-ianwatson","name":"IanWatson","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4_2.png","title":"Community Manager","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1512"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-01T12:52:09-08:00","id":1430688,"title":"","content":"Hello Devs<br /> <br /> Some time ago I made some tests with a friend so we could understand better the Combat Systems in practice, before we tried to actually Storyguide a session. We runned through the systems, made characters, rolled some combats, and everything worked ok... but a couple days later, we discovered that the book uses &quot;Unarmed&quot; as a Weapon that gives +1 Enhancement! In our test, we simply used Unarmed as giving no Enhancement at all, and all seemed to work fine. <br /> <br /> So, here's the question: is there any particular reason you chose to give +1 Enhancement to the &quot;Unarmed&quot; weapon, instead of none? We're kinda curious here, we probably missed something.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1001-timecrafter","name":"Timecrafter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1001_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"134"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-04T03:45:23-08:00","id":1430968,"title":"","content":"If Teleportation psi powers aren't capable of intergalactic travel. If a teleporter looked at, say, the Andromeda Galaxy and tried to make it there, how far do they go?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26448-shalmaneser","name":"Shalmaneser","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"79"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-04T03:50:12-08:00","id":1430969,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shalmaneser</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1362003-ask-a-dev?p=1430968#post1430968\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If Teleportation psi powers aren't capable of intergalactic travel. If a teleporter looked at, say, the Andromeda Galaxy and tried to make it there, how far do they go?</div> </div> </div> </div>They don\u2019t go anywhere. It\u2019s beyond their range so the power just fails.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-05T06:10:56-08:00","id":1431156,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>pcontop</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1362003-ask-a-dev?p=1420467#post1420467\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Could not find this asked before, so here it is:<br /> <br /> How does Dynamic Control work, in practice?<br /> <br /> What I get is this:<br /> <br /> You roll dynamically for it to be activated, then assign the uses for Mode electromagnetic broadcasts.<br /> <br /> &quot;Once activated, each laser or other beam functions on its own, but moving, altering, or redirecting more than one of these lasers per round requires a mixed action.&quot;<br /> <br /> What about the next turns, if you do not reassign anything, how many successes does it get on the attack? Do you roll for each attack separately and reflexively (with a full pool)? Or do you roll reflexively psi + mode + enhancements and assign successes for each task (defend, attack, wall, rework data) in a mixed roll? Or is the mixed roll to define successes for attacking, defending, etc, not reflexive? Or is it only non-reflexive when you reassign operations?</div> </div> </div> </div>Sorry, but I couldn't find an answer to this. Could you help me with the above question?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1524-pcontop","name":"pcontop","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1524_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"278"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-13T02:40:48-08:00","id":1432059,"title":"","content":"Psiads can combine multiple aptitudes, and Adaptability always tries to activate to protect a character from harm. Would a psiad with Adaptability be able to reflexively activate a defensive power from another aptitude if used as a combined effect? (Putting up a mind shield when about to be mind-controlled, or teleporting away, without prior activation of those powers, for example)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26448,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26448-shalmaneser","user":"Shalmaneser","date":". 01-13-2021, 05:48 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26448-shalmaneser","name":"Shalmaneser","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"79"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-13T04:56:18-08:00","id":1432070,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>pcontop</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1362003-ask-a-dev?p=1420467#post1420467\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Could not find this asked before, so here it is:<br /> <br /> How does Dynamic Control work, in practice?<br /> <br /> What I get is this:<br /> <br /> You roll dynamically for it to be activated, then assign the uses for Mode electromagnetic broadcasts. <br /> <br /> &amp;quot;Once activated, each laser or other beam functions on its own, but moving, altering, or redirecting more than one of these lasers per round requires a mixed action.&amp;quot;<br /> <br /> What about the next turns, if you do not reassign anything, how many successes does it get on the attack? Do you roll for each attack separately and reflexively (with a full pool)? Or do you roll reflexively psi + mode + enhancements and assign successes for each task (defend, attack, wall, rework data) in a mixed roll? Or is the mixed roll to define successes for attacking, defending, etc, not reflexive? Or is it only non-reflexive when you reassign operations?</div> </div> </div> </div>Sorry this took me so long to get back to, I\u2019d forgotten I hadn\u2019t answered it.<br /> <br /> Okay, Dynamic Control. First of all, ignore the reflexive part in the first line of the System, this requires a standard Psi activation roll, and there\u2019s no benefit to rolling a second time as you get a number of effects equal to Mode dots regardless of what your success is, and punishing failure after activation is undesirable.<br /> <br /> Activate the power - ordinary action, 2 Psi points, Psi + Mode dots. On success the psion gains a number of focused photokinetic effects (\u201clasers\u201d) equal to his Mode dots. These effects endure for one Scene and continue doing whatever the psion initially sets them to unless he changes them in a round. <br /> <br /> The psion can achieve various subtle displays with the power, but generally each \u2018laser\u2019 can be set to one of the following tasks:<br /> - Fire offensively as per Photonic Power<br /> - Work defensively, adding to defense.<br /> - Create a wall of light, providing an indirect damage barrier.<br /> <br /> I\u2019d say you can combine several \u2018lasers\u2019 to the same task as a single ordinary action, gaining +1 Enhancement for each additional laser so dedicated. Otherwise, you need to use mixed actions but each laser gets +1 Enhancement. So, if you had four lasers and had one set to defense and the other three firing at the same target, you\u2019d have a Photonic Power shot with +3 Enhancement beyond the usual description. If you set each of the lasers against different targets you\u2019ve have a three-action mixed action, each with +1 Enhancement. <br /> <br /> Directing or changing the focus of each \u2018laser\u2019 in a round requires an ordinary action (or a mixed action if doing more than one). <br /> <br /> Does that help?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-13T05:58:00-08:00","id":1432073,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bunyip</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1362003-ask-a-dev?p=1432070#post1432070\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> (...)<br /> <br /> Does that help?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> It does, thank you. But I will have to make two questions/clarifications:<br /> <br /> - What is it rolled to make the attack pool on each round, Psi + Mode? Is this attack roll reflexive or use an action?<br /> - Mixed actions work by allocating successes between the actions. How would changing the type of an effect work in a mixed action? One success per effect changed?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1524-pcontop","name":"pcontop","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1524_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"278"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-13T14:09:46-08:00","id":1432122,"title":"","content":"Hi! <br /> <br /> For Aberrant, can the players purchase the Impervious Tag for Toughness as well as the Environmental and Hard Armor tags?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2176-spectaculartentacular","name":"SpectacularTentacular","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2176_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"179"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-13T14:55:31-08:00","id":1432132,"title":"","content":"Also--Aberrants appear to be able to resist mental/emotional control, but not so much memory alteration, mental attacks, mental illusions, or telepathy. Am I missing something here?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2176-spectaculartentacular","name":"SpectacularTentacular","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2176_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"179"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-13T16:43:01-08:00","id":1432140,"title":"","content":"Another question: How can the Fighter Archetype for Novas get the Dreadful Presence Mega-Edge when they don't have the necessary dot in Mega-Presence? I can see the Overwhelming Denial Mega-Edge, or Subtle Presence, but not Dreadful Presence.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2176-spectaculartentacular","name":"SpectacularTentacular","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2176_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"179"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-14T11:12:47-08:00","id":1432228,"title":"","content":"Sorry if this has been answered elsewhere, but Pistols and Rifles appear at Scale 2 in the Aberrant book. Does this mean that firearms need to be treated as Scale 2 weapons? If so, what does that mean for armour?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26631-btriplem","name":"BtripleM","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-22T11:57:04-08:00","id":1433081,"title":"","content":"I have some questions about Boost<br /> <br /> If the variable power tag is applied, is there a limit on the number of times it can be activated? In other words, does the variable tag allow for activation applying to several attributes over several turns (or even the same turn with a mixed action?<br /> <br /> When applying the Extra Attributes how do you calculate the cost, particularly with relationship to the reduced cost power tag? It says that you multiply the Quantum point cost by the number of attributes affected. So if a nova has Boost with the Extra Attribute tag and the Reduced Cost (2) tag, what would be the cost of activating Boost for 2 attributes? Is it (Cost-1)*2=2 or is it (Cost*2)-1=3?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24929-econclark","name":"econclark","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-22T13:00:33-08:00","id":1433089,"title":"","content":"So not really a question but maybe. My group likes solid numbers or will ask for something a bit more solid then the scale chart. So I was looking at the speed table to get rough estimates on what each rank is roughly for speed, also so I as a SG have an understanding. I could easily be wrong here but a quick google search makes it look like the descriptor for 7-8 should be flipped. As escape velocity is around 40k kph and orbital velocity is around 27k kph. Is the wrong? I just did a quick google search.<br /> <br /> <br /> Also a Mega-Cunning question. On scale for imitative should I just run it as from a base of 1 across the boards and give everyone the 2 enhancement for every scale rank? Otherwise it seems like it would be a nightmare tracking differences between baselines and other novas.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6424-fuzzykuma","name":"Fuzzykuma","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6424_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"178"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-24T04:09:39-08:00","id":1433248,"title":"","content":"Lately, wht the telepath in the AEOn group, there have arisen some questions about whom can he contact (surface skim and deep scan, for example).<br /> <br /> How much aware of the character need the PC be? I mean, is in necessary to have any some kind of noetic connection, or just knowing someone is there, even if you have never het him before, is enough? (for example, you hear someone behind a closed door. Copuld the telpepath read his mind?)<br /> <br /> Another question is about range. Surface Skim states that it can be used at Mindscan range. Does it mean that Mindscan has to be activated before?<br /> <br /> Thanks!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26301-sothus","name":"Sothus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26301_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":1,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"15"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-24T14:17:18-08:00","id":1433301,"title":"","content":"What is the Xp value needed for Aberrant to make them equivalent to a Demi-God.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26393-shadowknyght","name":"shadowknyght","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-24T14:59:48-08:00","id":1433310,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>pcontop</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1362003-ask-a-dev?p=1432073#post1432073\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">- What is it rolled to make the attack pool on each round, Psi + Mode? Is this attack roll reflexive or use an action?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, Psi + Mode. If the laser continues to attack the same target each round, I\u2019d say it\u2019s reflexive.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> - Mixed actions work by allocating successes between the actions. How would changing the type of an effect work in a mixed action? One success per effect changed? </div> </div> </div>Yes, you need to spend one success to actions that don\u2019t require dice rolls in mixed actions.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-24T15:00:34-08:00","id":1433313,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>shadowknyght</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1362003-ask-a-dev?p=1433301#post1433301\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What is the Xp value needed for Aberrant to make them equivalent to a Demi-God.</div> </div> </div> </div>If you're asking about a direct comparison to Scion, there isn't one, as the two games are quite different. You'll have to come up with your own values, depending on the powers and abilities you want to mimic.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#800000\">Ian A. A. Watson</span></b><span style=\"color:#bdc3c7\">(he/she)</span><br /> <b>Onyx Path Community Manager<br /> Trinity Continuum Content Lead</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4-ianwatson","name":"IanWatson","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4_2.png","title":"Community Manager","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1512"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-24T15:06:17-08:00","id":1433316,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shalmaneser</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1362003-ask-a-dev?p=1432059#post1432059\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Psiads can combine multiple aptitudes, and Adaptability always tries to activate to protect a character from harm. Would a psiad with Adaptability be able to reflexively activate a defensive power from another aptitude if used as a combined effect? (Putting up a mind shield when about to be mind-controlled, or teleporting away, without prior activation of those powers, for example)</div> </div> </div> </div>I\u2019ve been debating with myself on this one. Overall, I think that yes, you could do this, but I can\u2019t really see the cost benefit to it. Adaptability requires sufficient dots to reflexively trigger the action. So you\u2019d need to activate Adaptability at the required level for the non-BK effect and keep it running. Using the Telepathy example, you\u2019d need one dot, which is simple enough. So you\u2019d activate the first dot of Adaptability and keep a Psi point committed to it, so that if you\u2019re later hit by a telepathic effect you can spend another Psi point to activate the shield. Why not just activate your shield and keep that psi point committed? <br /> <br /> The Psi Powers chapter in the upcoming <i>Prometheus Unbound</i> looks at combined Aptitudes in more detail. (As well as much more.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-24T15:11:56-08:00","id":1433317,"title":"","content":"Sorry. Please delete.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-24T15:13:35-08:00","id":1433318,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sothus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1362003-ask-a-dev?p=1433248#post1433248\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Lately, wht the telepath in the AEOn group, there have arisen some questions about whom can he contact (surface skim and deep scan, for example).<br /> <br /> How much aware of the character need the PC be? I mean, is in necessary to have any some kind of noetic connection, or just knowing someone is there, even if you have never het him before, is enough? (for example, you hear someone behind a closed door. Copuld the telpepath read his mind?)</div> </div> </div> </div>There\u2019s two answers to this. First, you\u2019d need to be able to see the target if you don\u2019t have a noetic connection to them. Just having a hunch that someone\u2019s on the other side of the door based on sound isn\u2019t enough. However, the second part is that you can use the Mindscan basic power first to detect minds around you - including the one on the other side of the door. This gives you a noetic connection that you can then use for other telepathic powers.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Another question is about range. Surface Skim states that it can be used at Mindscan range. Does it mean that Mindscan has to be activated before? </div> </div> </div>If you don\u2019t have line of sight, then yes, you need Mindscan active to give the noetic connection.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-27T01:08:23-08:00","id":1433585,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bunyip</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1362003-ask-a-dev?p=1433316#post1433316\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I\u2019ve been debating with myself on this one. Overall, I think that yes, you could do this, but I can\u2019t really see the cost benefit to it. Adaptability requires sufficient dots to reflexively trigger the action. So you\u2019d need to activate Adaptability at the required level for the non-BK effect and keep it running. Using the Telepathy example, you\u2019d need one dot, which is simple enough. So you\u2019d activate the first dot of Adaptability and keep a Psi point committed to it, so that if you\u2019re later hit by a telepathic effect you can spend another Psi point to activate the shield. Why not just activate your shield and keep that psi point committed?</div> </div> </div> </div>My guess was that it covers cases where you don't know what other mode might be useful- Telepathic attack? Up goes the mind shield. Someone nukes your town? Teleport away a few kilometers. It would seem to give the option of using any other power the character might happen to know reflexively in the cause of keeping your character alive without having to predict the nature of the threat or to even be fully aware of it. <br /> <br /> Also, in general, does Adaptability have to be activated first (with a psi point committed to keep it active) to keep it ready for a future threat, or will it activate itself in response to a threat if the psion/ad has sufficient psi points?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26448-shalmaneser","name":"Shalmaneser","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"79"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-27T01:51:05-08:00","id":1433587,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shalmaneser</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1362003-ask-a-dev?p=1433585#post1433585\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, in general, does Adaptability have to be activated first (with a psi point committed to keep it active) to keep it ready for a future threat, or will it activate itself in response to a threat if the psion/ad has sufficient psi points?</div> </div> </div> </div>Adaptation will try to activate in response to an appropriate threat. It still requires the successful psi roll, but in these instances the roll (and Psi point expenditure, if any) is reflexive.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-08T09:30:59-08:00","id":1434856,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-size:12px\">Trying to determine if this is a RAW legal Q-Tech Device*.</span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Thrillshot Aerial Duelist (Rank 5, 7 Nova Traits, 20 Edges, 6 Tags)</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Designed by English Megagenius Colby Thorn, the Thrillshot suit grants the Nova wearing it the ability to fly at subsonic speed with grace, while also providing solid protection from small arms.Consisting of a sealed novastolo suit and helmet, the Thrillshot utilizes microjets in the boots, back, arms, and hands to grant aerial speed and maneuverability. Though unarmed, the Thrillshot does not prevent the Nova from wielding hand-held weapons.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Mega-Attributes:</b> Mega-Dexterity 2</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Mega-Edges: </b>Toughness 2</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Quantum Powers:</b> Flight 3</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Durability Scale:</b> 2</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Edges:</b> Hair Trigger Reflexes, Keen Sense (Vision, Hearing), Sniper 3, Hardy 3, Tough Cookie 2</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Armor Tags:</b> Complete 3, Environmental 2, Soft 1</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Soft Armor Value:</b> 3 (Toughness, Tough Cookie, and Soft 1)</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Hard Armor Value:</b> 0</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Weaponry:</b> None</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Other:</b> Speed Scale 3 flight<br /> <br /> *I know that TC: Aberrant and TC: Core don't have the Environmental and Complete armor Tags)</span></span></span><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse.php?author=Sean%20Creef\" target=\"_blank\">Community Content Creator</a><a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse.php?author=Sean%20Creef\" target=\"_blank\"> - OPP Freelancer</a> - Storyguide / Storyteller<br /> Currently Running: Trinity Continuum Core, Vampire the Masquerade 5th Edition","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3331-tragedyjones","name":"tragedyjones","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"79"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-08T19:08:36-08:00","id":1434899,"title":"","content":"Question on speed scale for Aberrant. As in the book space speed goes up to a scale of 6. Earth to Mars in 30 minutes. What happens when a nova reaches quantum 6+ and can have space speed 7? <br /> <br /> On start a 150xp nova could have space speed 6 and a normal speed scale of 10 which is faster. <br /> <br /> Does the mega-dex speed still stack with flight? As written now it would not in the last backer PDF yet space speed still refutes to it as a speed boost for space flight.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6424-fuzzykuma","name":"Fuzzykuma","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6424_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"178"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-13T05:05:20-08:00","id":1435348,"title":"","content":"1) I've got a question about boosting Psi powers. If I've only got, for instance, Photokinesis 1 but I want to boost it to Photokinesis 3 (Photonic Power) to shoot a laser beam, do I calculate the effects of Photonic Power with my actual Mode rating of 1 (giving me 1 Enhancement and 1 tag/success) or the power's Mode rating of 3 (giving me 3 Enhancement and 3 tags/success)? <br /> <br /> 2) Can you apply Aim-based Edges such as Sniper or Trick Shooter to ranged attacks with psi powers like Photonic Power or Velocity, even though they don't actually use the Aim skill?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4009-wynterknight","name":"Wynterknight","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"22"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-13T16:22:40-08:00","id":1435402,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wynterknight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1362003-ask-a-dev?p=1435348#post1435348\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1) I've got a question about boosting Psi powers. If I've only got, for instance, Photokinesis 1 but I want to boost it to Photokinesis 3 (Photonic Power) to shoot a laser beam, do I calculate the effects of Photonic Power with my actual Mode rating of 1 (giving me 1 Enhancement and 1 tag/success) or the power's Mode rating of 3 (giving me 3 Enhancement and 3 tags/success)?</div> </div> </div> </div>You use the character\u2019s actual Mode rating.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 2) Can you apply Aim-based Edges such as Sniper or Trick Shooter to ranged attacks with psi powers like Photonic Power or Velocity, even though they don't actually use the Aim skill? </div> </div> </div>RAW no, but feel free to give it a try and see how it works for your table.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-21T07:22:30-08:00","id":1436403,"title":"","content":"Hi! I've got a question about the Biokinesis basic power Form Mastery. <br /> <br /> The text includes this line: &quot;Total the successes; extra Psi points (in addition to the powers\u2019 base costs) may be required to perform all the transformations in this shape.&quot; What does this mean? I don't see anything anywhere about spending extra Psi for additional benefits. In what case would you need to spend additional Psi points, outside of the powers' base costs?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4009-wynterknight","name":"Wynterknight","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"22"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-11T17:18:34-07:00","id":1443537,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-size:16px\">Quantum/2: should we round up or down?<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Powers like &quot;Quantum Attack&quot; (Aberrant p 219) and &quot;Quantum Construct&quot; (Aberrant p 220) refer to some parameter values to be equal to &quot;Quantum/2&quot;. Since these power descriptions do not tell us how to round these, and I couldn't find any guideline about default rounding in the book... what is the default rounding for Aberrant Trait divisions (especially Quantum)? Thank you!</span></span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1001-timecrafter","name":"Timecrafter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1001_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"134"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-11T17:24:33-07:00","id":1443538,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-size:16px\">Variable (X) Tag: examples</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Could you please give us some concrete examples of use of this tag? (Aberrant p 204). Thank you!!!</span></span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1001-timecrafter","name":"Timecrafter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1001_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"134"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-20T14:31:13-07:00","id":1444917,"title":"","content":"Apologies if this is an easy to answer question that I just overlooked, but does anyone know where the info on how hunger, thirst, etc. work is located? I've been digging through my TC:Core copy and I can't seem to find it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26317-critian-caceorte","name":"Critian Caceorte","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"246"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-20T22:34:32-07:00","id":1444995,"title":"","content":"Re: Psiad Attunement Range and Clairsentience or other effects that would increase psi for purposes of attunement range.<br /> <br /> The attunement radius for a psion continues to increase past an effective psi of 7 per their attunement range chart, which isn't the case on the chart listed for the psiad. Is the psiad's attunement radius stuck at a maximum of 10km?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26448-shalmaneser","name":"Shalmaneser","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"79"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-21T01:50:29-07:00","id":1445013,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shalmaneser</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1362003-ask-a-dev?p=1444995#post1444995\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Re: Psiad Attunement Range and Clairsentience or other effects that would increase psi for purposes of attunement range.<br /> <br /> The attunement radius for a psion continues to increase past an effective psi of 7 per their attunement range chart, which isn't the case on the chart listed for the psiad. Is the psiad's attunement radius stuck at a maximum of 10km?</div> </div> </div> </div>Increasing Attunement beyond Psi 7 works the same for psiads as it does for psions. Multiply by 10 for each dot over 7.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-21T06:27:48-07:00","id":1445037,"title":"","content":"I expected a full write-up of all prominent Aeon Society members like in 1E. Will we get this at a later date or is it not on the table?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8890-nullapostle","name":"NullApostle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-23T22:58:23-07:00","id":1445616,"title":"","content":"The level 5 Fundamentals power &quot;Transference&quot; can give an enhancement to any beings in the psion's radius with a psi trait. Since baseline humans have a psi trait of 1, does this apply to them as well?<br /> <br /> Also, Fundamentals can be used to remove Corruption. Is there a reasonable way for a Quantakinetic (perhaps in conjunction with other psions) to turn a corrupted Aberrant into an Eden-style non-corrupted Nova? I don't think we've gotten an explanation for what goes wrong mechanically with the Quantum to produce a corrupted quantum user.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26448,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26448-shalmaneser","user":"Shalmaneser","date":". 04-24-2021, 02:23 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26448-shalmaneser","name":"Shalmaneser","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"79"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-24T04:24:54-07:00","id":1445640,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shalmaneser</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1362003-ask-a-dev?p=1445616#post1445616\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The level 5 Fundamentals power &amp;quot;Transference&amp;quot; can give an enhancement to any beings in the psion's radius with a psi trait. Since baseline humans have a psi trait of 1, does this apply to them as well?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Also, Fundamentals can be used to remove Corruption. Is there a reasonable way for a Quantakinetic (perhaps in conjunction with other psions) to turn a corrupted Aberrant into an Eden-style non-corrupted Nova? I don't think we've gotten an explanation for what goes wrong mechanically with the Quantum to produce a corrupted quantum user. </div> </div> </div>As written, no. If you want it to work for your game you\u2019ll have to figure out the details.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-02T09:02:15-07:00","id":1446987,"title":"","content":"Looking at the backer manuscript for Trinity Continuum: Adventure! I noticed that it was missing the XP totals for building a more experienced character. Is it possible to get a preview of that? Also, what are the chances of getting an Adventure character sheet before the final release to make it easier to work up some test characters?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26811-uphill-gamer","name":"Uphill Gamer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26811_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-02T09:22:32-07:00","id":1446992,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Uphill Gamer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1362003-ask-a-dev?p=1446987#post1446987\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Looking at the backer manuscript for Trinity Continuum: Adventure! I noticed that it was missing the XP totals for building a more experienced character. Is it possible to get a preview of that?</div> </div> </div> </div>If there's something you feel is missing from the manuscript, please add it to the feedback form.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Also, what are the chances of getting an Adventure character sheet before the final release to make it easier to work up some test characters? </div> </div> </div>Character sheets are part of the layout process, so you'll see those when the backer PDF goes out.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#800000\">Ian A. A. Watson</span></b><span style=\"color:#bdc3c7\">(he/she)</span><br /> <b>Onyx Path Community Manager<br /> Trinity Continuum Content Lead</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4-ianwatson","name":"IanWatson","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4_2.png","title":"Community Manager","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1512"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-02T15:28:23-07:00","id":1447045,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>IanWatson</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1362003-ask-a-dev?p=1446992#post1446992\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> If there's something you feel is missing from the manuscript, please add it to the feedback form.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>The feedback form is closed. Is there another avenue where I could submit the missing information?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26811-uphill-gamer","name":"Uphill Gamer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26811_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-03T20:15:54-07:00","id":1447321,"title":"","content":"Not sure if this has been asked yet. It\u2019s for the system Devs. Is their a reason range was kept out of the scale system? It seems as though it would been part of scale or easily could have been. Just wondering. I can see possible reasons on both sides of a debate in why yes and why no.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6424-fuzzykuma","name":"Fuzzykuma","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6424_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"178"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-03T20:23:00-07:00","id":1447322,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fuzzykuma</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1362003-ask-a-dev?p=1447321#post1447321\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not sure if this has been asked yet. It\u2019s for the system Devs. Is their a reason range was kept out of the scale system? It seems as though it would been part of scale or easily could have been. Just wondering. I can see possible reasons on both sides of a debate in why yes and why no.</div> </div> </div> </div>For Aberrant we kept it limited to a handful of specific measurements. But as per the core rules, Scale can apply to pretty much any quality you want. So if you want to add a Range Scale, go for it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#800000\">Ian A. A. Watson</span></b><span style=\"color:#bdc3c7\">(he/she)</span><br /> <b>Onyx Path Community Manager<br /> Trinity Continuum Content Lead</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4-ianwatson","name":"IanWatson","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4_2.png","title":"Community Manager","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1512"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-04T06:47:06-07:00","id":1447397,"title":"","content":"When might details for the TC: Adventure Companion, especially &quot;The Adventure! Addendum - Strange New Life!,&quot; be available to backers? I am particularly eager to see what you all came up with.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#181818\"><span style=\"font-family:Merriweather\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">\u201cHumpty had always sat on walls, it was his way.\u201d </span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#181818\"><span style=\"font-family:Merriweather\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">\u2015 </span></span></span><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Lato\"><b><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Jasper Fforde, </span></b></span></span><span style=\"color:#181818\"><span style=\"font-family:Merriweather\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://www.goodreads.com/work/quotes/2504943\" target=\"_blank\">The Big Over Easy</a></span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":1756,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1756-mythadvocate","user":"MythAdvocate","date":". 05-04-2021, 09:50 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1756-mythadvocate","name":"MythAdvocate","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1756_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"444"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-04T08:33:46-07:00","id":1447407,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MythAdvocate</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1362003-ask-a-dev?p=1447397#post1447397\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">When might details for the TC: Adventure Companion, especially &quot;The Adventure! Addendum - Strange New Life!,&quot; be available to backers? I am particularly eager to see what you all came up with.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Probably won't hear much until after Adventure! itself is out.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#800000\">Ian A. A. Watson</span></b><span style=\"color:#bdc3c7\">(he/she)</span><br /> <b>Onyx Path Community Manager<br /> Trinity Continuum Content Lead</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4-ianwatson","name":"IanWatson","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4_2.png","title":"Community Manager","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1512"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-04T19:30:22-07:00","id":1447515,"title":"","content":"Hi!<br /> Canonically, during Hammersmith event, does Michael became a Stalwart or a Nova? And Sara, does she became a Mesmerist or a Psiad? \ud83e\udd14<br /> (I understand that probably no one could tell the difference at that point, but I'd like to know the canon version)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1001-timecrafter","name":"Timecrafter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1001_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"134"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-04T19:35:28-07:00","id":1447516,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Timecrafter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1362003-ask-a-dev?p=1447515#post1447515\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hi!<br /> Canonically, during Hammersmith event, does Michael became a Stalwart or a Nova? And Sara, does she became a Mesmerist or a Psiad? \ud83e\udd14<br /> (I understand that probably no one could tell the difference at that point, but I'd like to know the canon version)</div> </div> </div> </div>The labels are not neat little boxes. At the power levels involved, any distinction between &quot;powerful stalwart&quot; or &quot;nova&quot; would be immaterial.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#800000\">Ian A. A. Watson</span></b><span style=\"color:#bdc3c7\">(he/she)</span><br /> <b>Onyx Path Community Manager<br /> Trinity Continuum Content Lead</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4-ianwatson","name":"IanWatson","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4_2.png","title":"Community Manager","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1512"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-05T08:25:41-07:00","id":1447578,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>IanWatson</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1362003-ask-a-dev?p=1447516#post1447516\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The labels are not neat little boxes. At the power levels involved, any distinction between &quot;powerful stalwart&quot; or &quot;nova&quot; would be immaterial.</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean, in Adventure era, does Michael and Sarah have access to Dramatic Edit? In the same way (in-game) that Stalwarts and Mesmerists have, but Novas and Psiads do not? \ud83e\udd14<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1001-timecrafter","name":"Timecrafter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1001_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"134"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-05T09:49:41-07:00","id":1447591,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Timecrafter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1362003-ask-a-dev?p=1447578#post1447578\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I mean, in Adventure era, does Michael and Sarah have access to Dramatic Edit? In the same way (in-game) that Stalwarts and Mesmerists have, but Novas and Psiads do not? \ud83e\udd14</div> </div> </div> </div>Every non-baseline in the Adventure! era has access to dramatic editing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#800000\">Ian A. A. Watson</span></b><span style=\"color:#bdc3c7\">(he/she)</span><br /> <b>Onyx Path Community Manager<br /> Trinity Continuum Content Lead</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4-ianwatson","name":"IanWatson","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4_2.png","title":"Community Manager","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1512"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-06T20:22:47-07:00","id":1447757,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>IanWatson</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1362003-ask-a-dev?p=1447591#post1447591\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Every non-baseline in the Adventure! era has access to dramatic editing.</div> </div> </div> </div>Would it be accurate to interpret that as an aspect of the environment rather than inherent power Stalwarts and Mesmerists have, since even Novas and Psiads on Inspiration Age Earth have access to it?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-06T20:37:16-07:00","id":1447758,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1362003-ask-a-dev?p=1447757#post1447757\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Would it be accurate to interpret that as an aspect of the environment rather than inherent power Stalwarts and Mesmerists have, since even Novas and Psiads on Inspiration Age Earth have access to it?</div> </div> </div> </div>Non-baselines in the Adventure! era get access to Dramatic Editing. In other eras it's limited to Talents. From a production standpoint this is for fun emulation of the pulp genre. In-world, the specifics of why are up to you and your group. Dramatic Editing itself is semi-non-diagetic, so for me the production explanation is sufficient.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#800000\">Ian A. A. Watson</span></b><span style=\"color:#bdc3c7\">(he/she)</span><br /> <b>Onyx Path Community Manager<br /> Trinity Continuum Content Lead</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4-ianwatson","name":"IanWatson","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4_2.png","title":"Community Manager","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1512"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-07T10:10:07-07:00","id":1447828,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>IanWatson</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1362003-ask-a-dev?p=1447758#post1447758\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Non-baselines in the Adventure! era get access to Dramatic Editing. In other eras it's limited to Talents. From a production standpoint this is for fun emulation of the pulp genre. In-world, the specifics of why are up to you and your group. Dramatic Editing itself is semi-non-diagetic, so for me the production explanation is sufficient.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Got it. Can we say the same about Facets?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1001-timecrafter","name":"Timecrafter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1001_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"134"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-19T07:32:07-07:00","id":1448983,"title":"","content":"Since people are now getting their Aberrant sourcebooks, can we ask questions about it and get answers now? <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2176-spectaculartentacular","name":"SpectacularTentacular","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2176_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"179"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-19T07:41:16-07:00","id":1448985,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SpectacularTentacular</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1362003-ask-a-dev?p=1448983#post1448983\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Since people are now getting their Aberrant sourcebooks, can we ask questions about it and get answers now?</div> </div> </div> </div>People have been doing that in this very thread for months already.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#800000\">Ian A. A. Watson</span></b><span style=\"color:#bdc3c7\">(he/she)</span><br /> <b>Onyx Path Community Manager<br /> Trinity Continuum Content Lead</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4-ianwatson","name":"IanWatson","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4_2.png","title":"Community Manager","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1512"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-20T09:12:41-07:00","id":1449123,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>IanWatson</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1362003-ask-a-dev?p=1448985#post1448985\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> People have been doing that in this very thread for months already.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> As have I, but some questions seem to keep getting missed. Let's try them again:<br /> <br /> 1) As it stands now, it appears that novas have little to no defense against telepathy. There WAS a Mega-edge that protected against it and other mental attacks, but it went away. Is the Iron Will Edge and the Indomitable Merit supposed to interfere with having one's mind read, or is telepathy a vulnerable area to novas? Does Mega-Composure grant scale to resist telepathy, and if so, what Skill +Attribute is rolled against what to prove success or failure? <br /> <br /> 2) I notice that Armor from the Toughness Mega-Edge has a durability Scale rating. How does Scale affect the armor? If the armor is higher Scale, does it have a higher Soft armor rating? If it's 3+ higher than the attack Scale, does the attack do nothing? <br /> <br /> 3) Can the Impervious Tag be added to Toughness or Quantum Field? If so, why wasn't that listed? If not, why not? <br /> <br /> More as I think of them","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2176-spectaculartentacular","name":"SpectacularTentacular","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2176_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"179"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-22T01:18:04-07:00","id":1449234,"title":"","content":"If Doyen assist one another with psi powers, do they gain the bonuses psions do for combining aptitudes, or is this simply a trick engineered into the prometheus effect?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26448-shalmaneser","name":"Shalmaneser","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"79"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-23T22:47:47-07:00","id":1449424,"title":"","content":"Growth says a nova must \u201cpay the cost again\u201d when going from a smaller increased scale to a larger one (ie you went to size scale 3, but now want to go to 5). Does this mean you have to pay the full 5 QP to increase or just the difference of 2 QP?<br /> <br /> Can you use Healing to remove more than one Injury Condition in a single roll if you have enough successes? (ie you have Healing 2 and get 4 successes, can you remove 2 Injured or 4 Bruised from the same roll for the single QP?)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1885,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1885-crackedman","user":"CrackedMan","date":". 05-24-2021, 01:56 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1885-crackedman","name":"CrackedMan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1885_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"254"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-24T00:43:38-07:00","id":1449432,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shalmaneser</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1362003-ask-a-dev?p=1449234#post1449234\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If Doyen assist one another with psi powers, do they gain the bonuses psions do for combining aptitudes, or is this simply a trick engineered into the prometheus effect?</div> </div> </div> </div><i>Under Alien Skies</i> should help with this.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-24T09:54:26-07:00","id":1449467,"title":"","content":"I'm unsure about how the Feature of the Camaraderie Bond is actually useful - it provides the members of a group the short term ability to grant successes in a limited set of skills to other team members as 1-point enhancements, but this seems redundant (and more limited overall) with regards to the core mechanic's generic Enhanced Stunt ability, which lets any character spend extra successes to give themselves or any other character enhancement equal to the extra successes spent. Am I missing a benefit of the Camaraderie feature?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26850-warren-locke","name":"Warren Locke","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26850_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-27T18:06:13-07:00","id":1449896,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b>Mundane Weapons Power Scale</b></span><br /> <br /> Hi. Aberrant Scale Table (p.164) tells us that knives are intrinsically Power Scale 1, and that Pistols and Rifles are Power Scale 2.<br /> <br /> a) So, if a Baseline shoots a Pistol against another Baseline, that means the weapon should be considered Scale 2? How does it interact with the TC:Core Rules for Weapons? Are common Pistols Scale 2 or Scale 1 after all?<br /> <br /> Also, we know that you can't damage anything that is 3 or more Scales beyond yours (<i>&quot;The Bigger they are Gift&quot;</i>, Aberrant p.98, shows us how this works).<br /> <br /> b) So, if you have a Quantum Attack with Power (damage) Scale 1, we know there is a non-zero chance that you'll be able to damage something (or someone) with Durability Scale 3, but it's 100% guaranteed that you <i><b>cannot </b></i>damage anything of Scale 4, right?<br /> <br /> c) That said, picture a Nova with Durability Scale 4. <b>We know that he is 100% immune to baseline punches </b>(these are Scale 1, so he is 3 Scales higher than a common punch). <b>Is this nova 100% immune to Pistols too?</b> Or a mundane Pistol should be considered Scale 2, and therefore, a Nova should have at least 2+3 = Durability Scale 5 to be 100% immune to Pistols?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1001-timecrafter","name":"Timecrafter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1001_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"134"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-28T22:55:02-07:00","id":1450136,"title":"","content":"Is there a direct relation between Attribute dots and Scale in the Trinity Continuum? The scale examples show a Strongman and a Chess Grandmaster as Scale 2. Does this loosely translate to a minimum number of dots in the associated Might and Mental Attributes?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26811-uphill-gamer","name":"Uphill Gamer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26811_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-28T23:43:56-07:00","id":1450140,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Uphill Gamer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1362003-ask-a-dev?p=1450136#post1450136\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is there a direct relation between Attribute dots and Scale in the Trinity Continuum? The scale examples show a Strongman and a Chess Grandmaster as Scale 2. Does this loosely translate to a minimum number of dots in the associated Might and Mental Attributes?</div> </div> </div> </div>No. Something could be 5 dots of Might and Scale 1, while another thing is 2 dots but Scale 2. The 2 dot thing is just intrinsically more mighty than the 5 dot thing, but because the 5 dot thing is near the top of its potential it has a chance to competing with the 2 dot thing that\u2019s a relatively weak example of its type.<br /> <br /> But no amount of extra dots gives automatic Scale bump. The Chess Grandmaster probably has a Skill Trick related to chess that bumps their Scale to 2, the same as the strongman and Might tests.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-06T07:06:00-07:00","id":1451131,"title":"","content":"What I would like to have seen is the actual in-game stats for some if the inventions that were said to change the world (notably hyperfusion reactors, novastel, and eufiber). They were presented as coretech, but I dont know what the stats would look like, much less how to craft them without incorporating mega-edges and quantum powers.<br /> <br /> Similarly, would one crafting things cures for cancer? That was also presented as coretech, but I don't know how to model that without using a quantum power.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25790-sparda104","name":"Sparda104","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-09T10:38:02-07:00","id":1451458,"title":"","content":"I'm not sure if this has been asked and answered before but... we will be getting stats on the NPCs this time right?<br /> Specifically Mal and Pax but the others as well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1776-sidious","name":"Sidious","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1776_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"92"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-12T05:47:35-07:00","id":1451835,"title":"","content":"A few questions I would like clarification on:<br /> -Can novas buy the superior trait edge so they can have normal attributes at 6. Is it possible for a story guide to allow this for his games.<br /> -Mega stamina says novas have vastly increased lifespans but the books says ratings of 1 to 5 only give an extra 40 years of life then at rating 6+ you no longer age. This jump doesn\u2019t seem to make sense to me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26058-aeonstorm","name":"Aeonstorm","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-12T07:37:03-07:00","id":1451849,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aeonstorm</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1362003-ask-a-dev?p=1451835#post1451835\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A few questions I would like clarification on:<br /> -Can novas buy the superior trait edge so they can have normal attributes at 6. Is it possible for a story guide to allow this for his games.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, they have Scale instead. But if a Storyguide wants to allow it, that's up to them.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> -Mega stamina says novas have vastly increased lifespans but the books says ratings of 1 to 5 only give an extra 40 years of life then at rating 6+ you no longer age. This jump doesn\u2019t seem to make sense to me. </div> </div> </div>Okay? What's your question?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#800000\">Ian A. A. Watson</span></b><span style=\"color:#bdc3c7\">(he/she)</span><br /> <b>Onyx Path Community Manager<br /> Trinity Continuum Content Lead</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4-ianwatson","name":"IanWatson","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4_2.png","title":"Community Manager","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1512"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-12T08:37:49-07:00","id":1451860,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>IanWatson</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1362003-ask-a-dev?p=1451849#post1451849\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> No, they have Scale instead. But if a Storyguide wants to allow it, that's up to them.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Okay? What's your question?</div> </div> </div> </div>Oops sorry forgot to ask this. In regards to the mega stamina question is lifespan increase 40 years per dot of mega stamina or 40 years regardless of the rating until mega stamina 6 is reached. For example would a nova with mega stamina 5 have an extra lifespan of 200 years.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26058-aeonstorm","name":"Aeonstorm","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-12T15:13:35-07:00","id":1451915,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>IanWatson</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1362003-ask-a-dev?p=1451849#post1451849\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No, they have Scale instead. But if a Storyguide wants to allow it, that's up to them.</div> </div> </div> </div>So should we assume the core book is wrong when it states:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"font-family:serif\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">These Edges can only be purchased by characters </span></span><span style=\"font-family:serif\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">who are powered: talents, psions, psiads, <u>novas</u>, etc.</span></span> </div> </div> </div>or is there a rule I missed in the Aberrant book that overrules it?<br /> <br /> edit: Never mind. I found the new rule on page 183 of Aberrant.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25506,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25506-shepherdboi","user":"Shepherdboi","date":". 06-12-2021, 07:05 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25506-shepherdboi","name":"Shepherdboi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25506_1.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"364"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-12T18:09:33-07:00","id":1451931,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aeonstorm</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1362003-ask-a-dev?p=1451860#post1451860\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Oops sorry forgot to ask this. In regards to the mega stamina question is lifespan increase 40 years per dot of mega stamina or 40 years regardless of the rating until mega stamina 6 is reached. For example would a nova with mega stamina 5 have an extra lifespan of 200 years.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, 40 years per dot.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#800000\">Ian A. A. Watson</span></b><span style=\"color:#bdc3c7\">(he/she)</span><br /> <b>Onyx Path Community Manager<br /> Trinity Continuum Content Lead</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4-ianwatson","name":"IanWatson","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4_2.png","title":"Community Manager","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1512"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-14T13:19:28-07:00","id":1452213,"title":"","content":"I have a question about the toughness mega edge.<br /> Toughness 1 counts as wearing armour with soft 1 and complete 3. Does this mean the nova has scale 2 durability?<br /> <br /> So for example would then toughness 3 give scale 4 durability or does it only grant scale 3 durability?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26058-aeonstorm","name":"Aeonstorm","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-14T14:26:20-07:00","id":1452232,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aeonstorm</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1362003-ask-a-dev?p=1452213#post1452213\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have a question about the toughness mega edge.<br /> Toughness 1 counts as wearing armour with soft 1 and complete 3. Does this mean the nova has scale 2 durability?<br /> <br /> So for example would then toughness 3 give scale 4 durability or does it only grant scale 3 durability?</div> </div> </div> </div>No, Toughness specifically notes that it only increases Scale after the first dot. Toughness 1 is Scale 1 armor. Toughness 2 is Scale 2, Toughness 3 is Scale 3 and so on.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-15T16:03:12-07:00","id":1452386,"title":"","content":"Does the mega edge immunity work against radiation? If so would work against things like nanotech, prions. An expanded list of examples people have considered would be great.<br /> <br /> Also something I was curious about is what other books for the aberrant line are in development or going to be released.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26058,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26058-aeonstorm","user":"Aeonstorm","date":".  Additional questions 06-16-2021, 12:54 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26058-aeonstorm","name":"Aeonstorm","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-21T01:14:43-07:00","id":1453016,"title":"","content":"It may seam a stupid question at first but people is reading so different than me that I need to ask.<br /> <br /> Terrestrial x Non-Terrestrial tag in Environmental Anima may be interpreted as:<br /> <br /> A. Earth-Like x Non-Earth-Like<br /> B. Land-based x Non-Land-Based<br /> <br /> What is the right interpretation?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-01T18:02:54-07:00","id":1454024,"title":"","content":"Is Quantum Leap (Aberrant p.195) pre-requisite a Typo?<br /> t says Mega-Might 2, but the description also says what happens if you get this Edge and have Mega-Might 1.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1001-timecrafter","name":"Timecrafter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1001_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"134"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-03T10:49:01-07:00","id":1454141,"title":"","content":"Can a Vitakinetic with Psi 2 and Augendis 0 use &quot;Reinforce&quot; (Augendis 1), or &quot;Stoicism&quot; (Augendis 2)? If so, what's the Duration? Does the same logic apply to other &quot;Mode dots time duration&quot; Psi powers?<br /> <br /> Also, what would be the armor value given by Reinforce? Does the same logic apply to other &quot;value = Mode dots/2&quot; Psi powers?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1001-timecrafter","name":"Timecrafter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1001_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"134"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-03T15:08:04-07:00","id":1454157,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Timecrafter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1362003-ask-a-dev?p=1454141#post1454141\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can a Vitakinetic with Psi 2 and Augendis 0 use &amp;quot;Reinforce&amp;quot; (Augendis 1), or &amp;quot;Stoicism&amp;quot; (Augendis 2)?</div> </div> </div> </div>No, you need at least one dot in a Mode to access the rest of it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-05T16:32:18-07:00","id":1454312,"title":"","content":"Sorry to ask, but is there some kind of Scale chart for the Storypath system? I have a hard time picturing each level of scale for different things, especially Mega-Attributes in Aberrant.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25545-jollycooperative","name":"jollycooperative","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"27"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-05T18:33:26-07:00","id":1454318,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>jollycooperative</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1362003-ask-a-dev?p=1454312#post1454312\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sorry to ask, but is there some kind of Scale chart for the Storypath system? I have a hard time picturing each level of scale for different things, especially Mega-Attributes in Aberrant.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> There's a Scale example chart on p. 164 of Aberrant.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#800000\">Ian A. A. Watson</span></b><span style=\"color:#bdc3c7\">(he/she)</span><br /> <b>Onyx Path Community Manager<br /> Trinity Continuum Content Lead</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4-ianwatson","name":"IanWatson","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4_2.png","title":"Community Manager","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1512"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-06T10:01:35-07:00","id":1454354,"title":"","content":"do Psiads suffer Psionic Dysfunction? if so, how? (I have Aexpansion, already read it and know Psiad rules, but couldn't find anything about this particular issue).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1001-timecrafter","name":"Timecrafter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1001_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"134"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-06T16:13:30-07:00","id":1454389,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Timecrafter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1362003-ask-a-dev?p=1454354#post1454354\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">do Psiads suffer Psionic Dysfunction? if so, how? (I have Aexpansion, already read it and know Psiad rules, but couldn't find anything about this particular issue).</div> </div> </div> </div>They technically can, but it\u2019s very difficult for them as their Mode caps make it difficult and dots from any Mode in any Aptitude count towards preventing it. To gain dysfunction a psiad would have to deliberately keep all but one Mode at 1 dot, take the Strong Mode Edge in a primary Aptitude, and pump that one Mode up to 4 dots. <br /> <br /> In practice, it just doesn\u2019t happen for psiads and is an unexpected side effect of the artificial limitations of the Prometheus Process.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-11T06:36:19-07:00","id":1454683,"title":"","content":"can Proxies buy the &quot;Superior Trait&quot; Powered Edge? Does it mean they can get to level 7 in Attributes?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1001-timecrafter","name":"Timecrafter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1001_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"134"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-11T12:48:28-07:00","id":1454705,"title":"","content":"The Growth quantum power (Aberrant p. 212) states that the effective Mega-Might gained from Growth doesn't stack with existing Mega-Might.<br /> <br /> However, other powers that can grant Mega-Might (Density, Molecular Chameleon, Transformation etc.) don't seem to have this limitation. Is there a particular reason why Growth is different?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11237-jefepato","name":"Jefepato","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11237_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"557"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-14T21:56:48-07:00","id":1454945,"title":"","content":"In Under Alien Skies, the description of Doyen throwing very large rocks very fast (p184) seems to suggest that the Level 6 powers can only boost one aspect of a power- like Size scale, or Speed Scale, but not both (the example used was of a Size 4 object at speed [3] or a Size 5 object at speed [2], but no option to increase both Size and Space Speed.)<br /> <br /> This conflicts with earlier clarifications here of how Level 6 powers work. Which is correct?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26448-shalmaneser","name":"Shalmaneser","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"79"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-15T02:04:26-07:00","id":1454947,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shalmaneser</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1362003-ask-a-dev?p=1454945#post1454945\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In Under Alien Skies, the description of Doyen throwing very large rocks very fast (p184) seems to suggest that the Level 6 powers can only boost one aspect of a power- like Size scale, or Speed Scale, but not both (the example used was of a Size 4 object at speed [3] or a Size 5 object at speed [2], but no option to increase both Size and Space Speed.)<br /> <br /> This conflicts with earlier clarifications here of how Level 6 powers work. Which is correct?</div> </div> </div> </div>Level 6 powers can increase multiple aspects simultaneously but only one step per aspect. Please report the discrepancy to the errata form.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-15T08:08:57-07:00","id":1454968,"title":"","content":"As came up in another thread, there's some dispute about whether Soft Armor numbers stack. Some explicitly say they do, some explicitly say they don't, but what about those that say neither? If I'm wearing Eufiber with Soft Armor 2 and using Quantum Field that provides Soft Armor 3, is my Soft Armor now 5?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26949-deadmanwalking","name":"Deadmanwalking","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"79"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-15T19:14:52-07:00","id":1455004,"title":"","content":"If I have Attunement 4, I can start the Game with one Rank 4 Q-Tech item.<br /> <br /> If I have zero Attunement, but I do have Quantum 2 and the Q-Tech Mega-Edge 3, I can start the Game with one Rank 5 Q-Tech item.<br /> <br /> So... what if I have Quantum 2, Q-Tech Mega Edge 3, AND ALSO have Attunement 4? Does it mean I can Attune and start the game with 2+3+4 = one Rank 9 item? If not, what can I do with these?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1001-timecrafter","name":"Timecrafter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1001_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"134"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-20T08:14:28-07:00","id":1455259,"title":"","content":"Mega-Composure says that it removes Complications that result from 'emotional or social distractions' and then reduces the difficulty of Composure rolls. Is the Difficulty reduction somehow conditional? I mean, does it necessitate that there have been a Complication to start with, or only work if the Difficulty is due to 'emotional or social distractions' or would it just reduce Difficulty of Composure rolls no matter what? <br /> <br /> I had assumed the latter reading it (especially since Difficulty isn't usually given a 'type' like Complications are), but a lot of people assumed the former. So which is it?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26949-deadmanwalking","name":"Deadmanwalking","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"79"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-24T00:24:43-07:00","id":1455484,"title":"","content":"Okay, so the Mega-Lifting Mega-Edge seems obscenely powerful at a glance. Yes, you can't directly do damage with it, but since novas bend the laws of physics, ignoring the need for leverage and such, it would appear that a nova that boosts their Might scale for lifting to even just a 6 could lift a small city. I can't help but think there's something I'm missing, perhaps in the difficulty of the roll itself. It feels like a beginning character, if built right, could heft up a city, then drop it, which honestly would be cataclysmic for the city.<br /> <br /> From beginning to end, including difficulties, and spending successes on stunts, what would it take for a character with Might scale 6 to lift a scale 6 small city?<br /> <br /> What would it take for a character that used Mega-Lifting to boost their Might scale to 9 to lift a scale 6 small city?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I\u2019m a writer. A storyteller. They\u2019re my passions. They\u2019re what I do. The stories I tell, they are my mythologies. Like the Norse tales of Odin, Thor, and Loki, or the Celtic fables of Lugh or C\u00fa Chulainn, I want them to be the kind that people retell. They are the legacies I wish to leave behind.","edited":{"userid":577,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/577-archasimos","user":"Archasimos","date":". 07-24-2021, 05:00 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/577-archasimos","name":"Archasimos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar577_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"180"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-24T00:44:31-07:00","id":1455486,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Archasimos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1362003-ask-a-dev?p=1455484#post1455484\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Okay, so the Mega-Lifting Mega-Edge seems obscenely powerful at a glance. Yes, you can't directly do damage with it, but since novas bend the laws of physics, ignoring the need for leverage and such, it would appear that a nova that boosts their Mega-Might for lifting to even just a 6 could lift a small city. I can't help but think there's something I'm missing, perhaps in the difficulty of the roll itself. It feels like a beginning character, if built right, could heft up a city, then drop it, which honestly would be cataclysmic for the city.<br /> <br /> From beginning to end, including difficulties, and spending successes on stunts, what would it take for a character with Mega-Might 6 to lift a scale 6 small city?<br /> <br /> What would it take for a character that used Mega-Lifting to boost their Mega-Might to 9 to lift a scale 6 small city?</div> </div> </div> </div>This seems more like a general community question than \u2018Ask a Dev\u2019.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-24T01:10:46-07:00","id":1455492,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bunyip</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1362003-ask-a-dev?p=1455486#post1455486\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This seems more like a general community question than \u2018Ask a Dev\u2019.</div> </div> </div> </div>I can do that if it's preferred. The original post about Ask a Dev wasn't terribly clear on what may or may not want to be discussed here. My ST is about to run two separate simultaneous games of Aberrant that exist side by side and I noticed that Mega-Lifting could technically be used to allow a starting character with Mega-Might 4 to achieve for instance a Might scale 9 for just lifting, and it seemed like this is either broken to the point where it could derail games (assuming the ST didn't just disallow such things for the sake of the game), or are we were missing something critical that would make it a lot harder than it appears.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I\u2019m a writer. A storyteller. They\u2019re my passions. They\u2019re what I do. The stories I tell, they are my mythologies. Like the Norse tales of Odin, Thor, and Loki, or the Celtic fables of Lugh or C\u00fa Chulainn, I want them to be the kind that people retell. They are the legacies I wish to leave behind.","edited":{"userid":577,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/577-archasimos","user":"Archasimos","date":". 07-24-2021, 04:59 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/577-archasimos","name":"Archasimos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar577_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"180"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-24T18:02:52-07:00","id":1455548,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Archasimos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1362003-ask-a-dev?p=1455492#post1455492\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I can do that if it's preferred. The original post about Ask a Dev wasn't terribly clear on what may or may not want to be discussed here.</div> </div> </div> </div>As a Dev is generally for clarification on how the system works, what the intent is behind certain rules or how they\u2019re meant to be interpreted, or clarification on elements of the setting. If you post here you\u2019ll often be waiting longer for an answer because the devs are busy working on projects and may not get to the forum or the thread for a while. In this thread it\u2019s also not allowed for the general community to pop in with their answers, suggestions, and opinions. If you want discussion or examples on how things work in gameplay, asking a question or making a thread outside Ask a Dev is usually the better choice because members of the community who have played countless hours of the game will chime in, and have probably encountered the same thing you\u2019re asking, or something similar.<br /> <br /> Hopefully that helps clarify it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-01T13:34:00-07:00","id":1455948,"title":"","content":"1) Do Q-Tech items gained during character creation (through Attunement or Q-Tech Mega Edge) start with Flaws?<br /> 2) If yes, how many? Can I &quot;buy them off&quot; to start Flawless? (or with less Flaws?)<br /> 3) If not, can I get Flaws to make this starting Q-Tech better (maybe working like Negative Tags)? How should I proceed?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1001-timecrafter","name":"Timecrafter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1001_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"134"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-01T19:17:51-07:00","id":1455983,"title":"","content":"Devs, please... I've read the Superscience Core rules and the Q-Tech rules over and over, but I simply couldn't understand how do you go from &quot;Rank 7, Maximum Enhancement 9, up to 30 dots (all types) but no more than 12 dots in Quantum Abilities, Maximum Tag Bonus 8&quot; to the Cyber Suit stats listed in Aberrant's Q-Tech table at pp. 243. Could you please clarify the step-by-step of how it's done? How do you actually &quot;spend&quot; these points to generate the stats listed in the Q-Tech Devices Example tables? If possible, please do the same to the the &quot;Teleportation Device&quot; and to the &quot;Intelligent Car&quot; (same table), because I really need your help here. Thank you!<br /> <br /> PS: I really hope you can explain Q-tech points allocation here (and Core game Super-Science also, in fact); my Aberrant game preparation hitted a standstill because of this. I'm a backer in all 4 kickstarters, I've read all the 3 hardcovers but I really still don't know what to say to my would-be-gadgeteer players. :/ We didn't use Super-Science crafting in our Core game, but its not a good choice to do in our Aberrant chronicle, because... gadgeteer player characters. \ud83d\ude2d","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1001,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1001-timecrafter","user":"Timecrafter","date":". 08-02-2021, 04:48 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1001-timecrafter","name":"Timecrafter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1001_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"134"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-03T22:18:19-07:00","id":1456103,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Warren Locke</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1362003-ask-a-dev?p=1449467#post1449467\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm unsure about how the Feature of the Camaraderie Bond is actually useful - it provides the members of a group the short term ability to grant successes in a limited set of skills to other team members as 1-point enhancements, but this seems redundant (and more limited overall) with regards to the core mechanic's generic Enhanced Stunt ability, which lets any character spend extra successes to give themselves or any other character enhancement equal to the extra successes spent. Am I missing a benefit of the Camaraderie feature?</div> </div> </div> </div>Just reposting this, as I think it may have been overlooked previously.<br /> <br /> I'd also like to add my voice to the previous poster's request for a general review of how the actual specific details of Q-Tech item point expenditure (and, really, Novatech too) work for an inventor Aberrant, as I also have a gadgeteer character and we've struggled pretty mightily with the systems as written. It just all seems very vague.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26850-warren-locke","name":"Warren Locke","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26850_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-04T10:38:31-07:00","id":1456140,"title":"","content":"I also have a gadgeteer player, and I didn't understand the rules of the books. [Core and Q-tech]","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26537-jonnes-derik","name":"Jonnes.Derik","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26537_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"74"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-05T14:58:22-07:00","id":1456202,"title":"","content":"I don't understand how Transportal 1: Window works.<br /> <br /> It costs 1 psi and an action, for which you can open two small portals which last for duration. How can this be used defensively/offensively? Can it be used relexively, costing 1 psi each use? Or Can you reflexively switch windows as you like while the port lasts (though this contradicts the sentence &quot;can\u2019t be moved once created&quot;)?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3122-shuragil","name":"shuragil","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"41"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-06T02:14:48-07:00","id":1456221,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>shuragil</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1362003-ask-a-dev?p=1456202#post1456202\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How can this be used defensively/offensively?</div> </div> </div> </div>Mixed actions. Not reflexively.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-06T15:08:06-07:00","id":1456268,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bunyip</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1362003-ask-a-dev?p=1456221#post1456221\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Mixed actions. Not reflexively.</div> </div> </div> </div>I can follow this when using Window for attacks. But I still don't get it when using it for defense, which _is_ some kind of reflexive roll, if i understand combat rules correctly. I mean, when opening a window as part of an earlier action, the opponent can easily step aside the window. He needs to be surpised by the suddenly appearing window to be effective for defense, which is probably not the case if it popped up a second or so earlier.<br /> <br /> Also Window, costing both 1 psi as well as the dice-loss of a mixed action _each time_ feels lackluster e.g. compared to Blink, which grants effects for several rounds after activation. At least I feel that way currently.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3122-shuragil","name":"shuragil","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"41"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-06T20:59:57-07:00","id":1456277,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>shuragil</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1362003-ask-a-dev?p=1456268#post1456268\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But I still don't get it when using it for defense, which _is_ some kind of reflexive roll, if i understand combat rules correctly.</div> </div> </div> </div>On your action, you activate Window. This could be your action, or part of a mixed action. If you're activating it with defense in mind, it thereafter makes it harder for enemies to damage you. If you're attacked before this in a round, you roll your Defense as normal, Window won't help you yet.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I mean, when opening a window as part of an earlier action, the opponent can easily step aside the window. He needs to be surpised by the suddenly appearing window to be effective for defense, which is probably not the case if it popped up a second or so earlier. </div> </div> </div>If you were carrying a shield, would you give it to your opponent and then complain that the opponent doesn't just spend their time hitting the shield instead of holding it to one side and hitting you? Why would you make defensive windows appear near the opponent? You put them near yourself so the opponent has less chance of hitting you, and more chance of their attack going through a window.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> feels lackluster e.g. compared to Blink </div> </div> </div>With respect, so what? Teleporters already have Blink as part of their toolkit. Aptitudes aren't designed to overlap 1:1, if at all. If a teleporter wants the good defensive power, take Translocation. If they want to cobble together a defensive use out of a more utilitarian ability, take Transportal. If the player decides to concentrate on Transportal and not take Translocation, that's their choice.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-08T14:13:58-07:00","id":1456371,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bunyip</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1362003-ask-a-dev?p=1456277#post1456277\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you were carrying a shield, would you give it to your opponent and then complain that the opponent doesn't just spend their time hitting the shield instead of holding it to one side and hitting you? Why would you make defensive windows appear near the opponent? You put them near yourself so the opponent has less chance of hitting you, and more chance of their attack going through a window.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ok, I didn't see it that way. The defensive effect of Window lasts the entire duration, as long as you can manage to stay near your &quot;shield&quot;. The offensive effect would still only count for one (mixed) activation, given that the opponent would step aside the window pointing in his direction. If there ever comes a revisited Aeon edition, I'd wish that a scenario like this is included, because a dumb like me isn't able to get this idea out of the written rules myself. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Thanks Bunyip!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3122-shuragil","name":"shuragil","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"41"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-14T11:52:15-07:00","id":1456820,"title":"","content":"Does &quot;Close Range&quot; (Core p.80) is 0-2m, or 0-3m? Since Short is listed as 3-30m? \ud83e\udd14<br /> Same doubt about Short (3-30m) versus Medium (31-100m). What are the correct numbers?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1001-timecrafter","name":"Timecrafter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1001_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"134"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-14T17:10:18-07:00","id":1456841,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Timecrafter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1362003-ask-a-dev?p=1456820#post1456820\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Does &amp;quot;Close Range&amp;quot; (Core p.80) is 0-2m, or 0-3m? Since Short is listed as 3-30m? \ud83e\udd14<br /> Same doubt about Short (3-30m) versus Medium (31-100m). What are the correct numbers?</div> </div> </div> </div>What\u2019s printed in the book is correct.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-15T17:21:25-07:00","id":1456915,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bunyip</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1362003-ask-a-dev?p=1456841#post1456841\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> What\u2019s printed in the book is correct.</div> </div> </div> </div>Please, clarify. My book - Core p.80 - literally says in the table: &quot;Close Range = 0-2m&quot; and &quot;Short Range = 3-30m&quot;.<br /> If my target is at 2,5m from me, is he at Close Range or Short Range?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1001-timecrafter","name":"Timecrafter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1001_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"134"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-15T19:21:06-07:00","id":1456923,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Timecrafter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1362003-ask-a-dev?p=1456915#post1456915\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Please, clarify. My book - Core p.80 - literally says in the table: &amp;quot;Close Range = 0-2m&amp;quot; and &amp;quot;Short Range = 3-30m&amp;quot;.<br /> If my target is at 2,5m from me, is he at Close Range or Short Range?</div> </div> </div> </div>Just decide. If you\u2019re worried about this level of nitpicking, you\u2019re not getting the kind of system Storypath is.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-16T03:50:52-07:00","id":1456946,"title":"","content":"For what it's worth, I tend to read the upper ends of ranges as being hard caps; so 0\u20132 and 3\u201330 actually mean \u201cup to 2\u201d and \u201cup to 30\u201d to my way of reading it. <br /> <br /> Not that I've ever encountered a situation where someone is 2\u00bd meters away, mind you; in practice, we tend to start with \u201cwhat range band are you in?\u201d and establish actual distances, if at all, based on that. We leave precise measurements of distance to games like D&amp;D.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-16T04:48:02-07:00","id":1456951,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1362003-ask-a-dev?p=1456946#post1456946\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">in practice, we tend to start with \u201cwhat range band are you in?\u201d and establish actual distances, if at all, based on that.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is exactly how it should be approached. &quot;How far away is the target?&quot; &quot;Eh, they're in short range.&quot;<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-23T23:52:15-07:00","id":1457554,"title":"","content":"[Aeon] Two questions:<br /> <br /> Does a psionic effect count as each of the modes used in that effect? For example, if a Quantakinetic uses Resist to protect himself against the Telekinesis mode, is he also protected if a psion uses a flaming hammer effect that combines Telekinesis and Thermokinesis?<br /> <br /> Can the Empowerment vitakinetic power grant temporary copies of Psionic edges which can only be taken once? For example, if the target has Favored Mode in one mode, could Empowerment grant it to a different mode of that psion? Could it &quot;double up&quot; to grant a +4 Enhancement to that already Favored mode?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26448-shalmaneser","name":"Shalmaneser","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"79"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-24T00:34:10-07:00","id":1457555,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shalmaneser</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1362003-ask-a-dev?p=1457554#post1457554\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">[Aeon] Two questions:<br /> <br /> Does a psionic effect count as each of the modes used in that effect? For example, if a Quantakinetic uses Resist to protect himself against the Telekinesis mode, is he also protected if a psion uses a flaming hammer effect that combines Telekinesis and Thermokinesis?</div> </div> </div> </div>As a broad general answer I\u2019d say yes, but it\u2019s going to be depend on the specifics of the power effect and what contribution the resisted Mode gives. It\u2019ll be SG\u2019s call, but some cases will have partial or minimal resistance.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Can the Empowerment vitakinetic power grant temporary copies of Psionic edges which can only be taken once? For example, if the target has Favored Mode in one mode, could Empowerment grant it to a different mode of that psion? Could it &amp;quot;double up&amp;quot; to grant a +4 Enhancement to that already Favored mode? </div> </div> </div>No.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-07T20:15:30-07:00","id":1459240,"title":"","content":"We had something come up during our Aberrant game today. When you have Quantum Attack with the Non Lethal option or another unusual tag, like Entangle, how does the increased Scale granted by Quantum Attack ranks beyond 1 apply?<br /> <br /> On the Inflict Damage stunt, the core rules say you just duplicate the stunt multiple times, when you have scale, but don't say how it impacts any other stunt, so it's unclear whether it just works the same way or not.<br /> <br /> <br /> Edit: Ok after having looked through the books a bit more, it seems like we were very confused about about how it works, so I'm gonna just lay it out here to see if I'm getting this right. I'll use someone with Mega Might throwing a punch, while wearing a cestus.<br /> <br /> First you roll your attack pool, in this case Close Combat+Might. If you get 1 or more successes, you add any enhancement from the weapon. Assuming you equal the target's defense, you can spend any remaining successes on any of the stunts you can afford.<br /> <br /> If you have Scale on your opponent, twice the difference in your Power Scale vs their Defense scale is also added as enhancement to your attack, right? <br /> <br /> And if you have the Non-Lethal Tag, that says that it applies the Stunned status...but the Stunned Status can't usually be bought as a Stunt, so how does that work? Is it just &quot;Use the Inflict Injury Stunt, except you're applying the Stunned Status instead of the Injury Status?&quot; If so, do I have to buy the Inflict Injury stunt multiple times to get the Unconsciousness Status?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":226,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","user":"BrilliantRain","date":". 09-23-2021, 12:13 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-24T08:20:43-07:00","id":1461219,"title":"","content":"We had these days the first combat in our Aeon game and several questions arose that I hope can be clarified here.<br /> <br /> 1) Armor<br /> 1a) Do two or more pieces of worn armor stack (in terms of soft/hard armor and in terms of other tags)? Say, a bioweave and a shifting armor, and maybe a VES on top of that.<br /> 1b) Does armor from different sources stack? E.g. a bioweave and a kinetic shield.<br /> 1c) In Core and Aeon are several references to an armor rating and an armor value (e.g. Core pp. 63 and 124, Aeon pp. 274, 262)? Is this meant to be soft armor? Or tags?<br /> 1d) Related to this, there are also several references to soft armor or soft armor value/rating without giving the type of resisted damage (e.g. Core p. 64, Aeon pp 126,127, 263). Do I have to choose the type (bulletproof, impact-resistant, slash-resistant, something else)? Or is it against any damage?<br /> <br /> 2) The Aim: shoot to injure skill trick (Core p 46) applies if the opponent takes an injury condition. But antagonists do not take injury conditions. How is this supposed to work? Also, I am wondering if it should really be possible to take out a main adversiary with just a single shot.<br /> <br /> 3) Weapons with the stun tag impose the stunned condition with a +2 complication. Does this mean that this stunned condition can be shaken off with a stamina+resolve roll with difficulty 2? Can I roll every round? And does it wear off naturally after 2 rounds?<br /> <br /> Thank you for your time!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27086-donaeva","name":"Donaeva","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-24T17:08:05-07:00","id":1461281,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Donaeva</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1362003-ask-a-dev?p=1461219#post1461219\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">We had these days the first combat in our Aeon game and several questions arose that I hope can be clarified here.<br /> <br /> 1) Armor<br /> 1a) Do two or more pieces of worn armor stack (in terms of soft/hard armor and in terms of other tags)? Say, a bioweave and a shifting armor, and maybe a VES on top of that.</div> </div> </div> </div>No.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 1b) Does armor from different sources stack? E.g. a bioweave and a kinetic shield. </div> </div> </div>Yes<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 1c) In Core and Aeon are several references to an armor rating and an armor value (e.g. Core pp. 63 and 124, Aeon pp. 274, 262)? Is this meant to be soft armor? Or tags? </div> </div> </div>If it doesn\u2019t specify, assume it\u2019s referring to Soft armor unless context makes it clear it\u2019s referring to Hard.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 1d) Related to this, there are also several references to soft armor or soft armor value/rating without giving the type of resisted damage (e.g. Core p. 64, Aeon pp 126,127, 263). Do I have to choose the type (bulletproof, impact-resistant, slash-resistant, something else)? Or is it against any damage? </div> </div> </div>If it doesn\u2019t specify, assume it\u2019s Complete unless context implies otherwise. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 2) The Aim: shoot to injure skill trick (Core p 46) applies if the opponent takes an injury condition. But antagonists do not take injury conditions. How is this supposed to work? Also, I am wondering if it should really be possible to take out a main adversiary with just a single shot. </div> </div> </div>Shoot to Injure is unbalanced and doesn\u2019t conform to the Skill Trick rules on p.45. I\u2019d recommend not allowing it. As written, it either does nothing against Antagonists or eliminates them in one shot regardless of their threat.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 3) Weapons with the stun tag impose the stunned condition with a +2 complication. Does this mean that this stunned condition can be shaken off with a stamina+resolve roll with difficulty 2? Can I roll every round? And does it wear off naturally after 2 rounds? </div> </div> </div>It\u2019s been a while since I looked into Stunned, but I believe so. (I may need to edit this part of the post when I have a chance to reread.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-07T01:56:06-07:00","id":1462985,"title":"","content":"Thanks Bunyip for the clarifications! I have another question <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> I am confused on some aspects of Aberrants as antagonists in Aeon.<br /> <br /> 1) Corruption: I understood that there is a corruption rating and a corruption pool. From the pool the Aberrant can spent points as described on p. 331 in Aeon. On p. 330 it says &quot;Corruption creates a pool equal to the rating [...] As a rough guideline, a suitable Corruption pool is equal to the number of players + the average Psi Rating of the group + Archetype Level of the Aberrant facing them.&quot; Initially I thought that the corruption rating is given by the Archetype (e.g. corruption 1 for sub-abberants, therefore pool 1), but the text seems to imply that the rating is actually given by the pool (say 4 players with psi 3 against a divergent with corruption 2 = corruption pool 9 = corruption rating 9)? Anyway, what exactly is the corruption rating for? I know the text says &quot;a static<br /> value for resisting powers&quot; but what does this mean? Can you give an example?<br /> <br /> 2) Power clash: On p. 330 in Aeon: &quot; For the purposes of psi powers, a Clash is resolved by making opposed Skill + Applicable Aptitude rolls; this is a Desperation pool for sub-Aberrant mutants, Secondary pool for Divergents and Nemeses, and a Primary pool for Terats.&quot; I honestly have no idea how to choose the skill and aptitude here. Assume an Aberrant is attacking with Disruption (p.335 in Aeon) to inflict an injury. A psion can resist this with a clash. What would be an applicable skill + aptitude?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27086-donaeva","name":"Donaeva","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-13T18:01:28-07:00","id":1463767,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Donaeva</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1362003-ask-a-dev?p=1462985#post1462985\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thanks Bunyip for the clarifications! I have another question <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> I am confused on some aspects of Aberrants as antagonists in Aeon.<br /> <br /> 1) Corruption: I understood that there is a corruption rating and a corruption pool. From the pool the Aberrant can spent points as described on p. 331 in Aeon. On p. 330 it says &quot;Corruption creates a pool equal to the rating [...] As a rough guideline, a suitable Corruption pool is equal to the number of players + the average Psi Rating of the group + Archetype Level of the Aberrant facing them.&quot; Initially I thought that the corruption rating is given by the Archetype (e.g. corruption 1 for sub-abberants, therefore pool 1), but the text seems to imply that the rating is actually given by the pool (say 4 players with psi 3 against a divergent with corruption 2 = corruption pool 9 = corruption rating 9)? Anyway, what exactly is the corruption rating for? I know the text says &quot;a static<br /> value for resisting powers&quot; but what does this mean? Can you give an example?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, that's confusing. Aberrants have a Corruption rating, and a Corruption Pool. The Corruption rating is what's referred to in the first instance and corresponds to the type of Aberrant, like youve said. The Corruption pool is calculated (as a suggestion) by the formula on page 330. <br /> <br /> The Corruption trait is used where a power or ability needs to overcome a Difficulty, or be resisted by, the target's Psi (or power trait). In these instances, use Corruption Trait in its place. Also, Aberrants are walking Corruption zones, so feel free to use the Aberrant's Corruption trait with the rules of pages 191-193 to inflict additional difficulty on psions using their powers in directly against the Aberrant.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 2) Power clash: On p. 330 in Aeon: &quot; For the purposes of psi powers, a Clash is resolved by making opposed Skill + Applicable Aptitude rolls; this is a Desperation pool for sub-Aberrant mutants, Secondary pool for Divergents and Nemeses, and a Primary pool for Terats.&quot; I honestly have no idea how to choose the skill and aptitude here. Assume an Aberrant is attacking with Disruption (p.335 in Aeon) to inflict an injury. A psion can resist this with a clash. What would be an applicable skill + aptitude? </div> </div> </div>As this is clashing Quantum and psi powers against each other, Psi + appropriate Mode would be the dice pool. The Aberrant section was written in parallel with the psi powers section and references the Skill + Aptitude mechanic from before the constant Psi + Mode foruma was settled.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-18T20:16:51-07:00","id":1464455,"title":"","content":"Hi, just got the core book. Real nice hardcover, by the way. Perfect size, too.<br /> <br /> So anyways I've got some questions about Super-Science. From reading the actual rules it seems like a Device of low rank should only have access to Edges, potentially. But the example Devices has a rank 1 set of spy glasses that have a Gift effect. Is that correct? Does &quot;Edge&quot; also include Gifts? Could I potentially make a rank 1 smartphone that has the &quot;Always Connected&quot; Gift and have a phone that can work anywhere?<br /> <br /> Also, when making a rank 1 Device how do you deal with the 4 stages of item creation? You have a minimum amount of Milestones of 1 for creating a rank 1 Device, so do you make 4 different roles during 1 Milestone or do you need 4 Milestones to account for the 4 stages of Item creation?<br /> <br /> Edit<br /> <br /> Oh, another question. When you determine your initial Gifts are you limited to the keywords for each path? Like if you have the Adventurer Origin Path does the Gift you get for that Path have have the Might, Pilot or Survival Keywords? Or can you choose any three Gifts as long as you have unlocked it's Keyword with one of your Paths? Like can I pick 3 Athletics Gifts if I've unlocked the Athletics Keyword with one path even though I might only have one Path that has the Athletics Keyword? Or can I only have an Athletics Gift for the Path that has the the associated skill?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":27133,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27133-planguy","user":"Planguy","date":". 10-20-2021, 12:00 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27133-planguy","name":"Planguy","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"111"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-20T21:00:20-07:00","id":1464685,"title":"","content":"In Aberrant, how do the Modular rules work?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-23T15:51:10-07:00","id":1465054,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BrilliantRain</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1362003-ask-a-dev?p=1464685#post1464685\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In Aberrant, how do the Modular rules work?</div> </div> </div> </div>Not trying to be flippant, but they work according to the rules in TC: Aberrant. I don\u2019t know what you\u2019re asking.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-23T17:36:23-07:00","id":1465069,"title":"","content":"The Transformation power from page 224 of Aberrant says it costs, &quot;1 Quantum point per dot distributed&quot; while the Extra Traits power tag says, &quot;Each instance of this tag increases Transformation's Cost by 1 Quantum point.&quot;<br /> <br /> If a character has Transformation 3 and one Extra Traits power tag and allocates all six of the available power dots, which of the following is true?<br /> <br /> 1). The character spends 7 Quantum; 3 from dots granted by Transformation, 3 from dots granted by Extra Traits, and 1 from possessing the Extra Traits tag.<br /> <br /> 2). The character spends 4 Quantum; 3 from dots granted by Transformation and 1 from possessing the Extra Traits tag, with the 3 dots granted by Extra Traits not having an extra cost.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25506-shepherdboi","name":"Shepherdboi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25506_1.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"364"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-27T01:06:10-07:00","id":1465486,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shepherdboi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1362003-ask-a-dev?p=1465069#post1465069\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1). The character spends 7 Quantum; 3 from dots granted by Transformation, 3 from dots granted by Extra Traits, and 1 from possessing the Extra Traits tag.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd say this one.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-30T03:29:14-07:00","id":1465880,"title":"","content":"The &quot;Life of Privilege&quot; origin path has only 13 points worth of Edges. Fame=3, Patron=3, Skilled Liar=2, Wealth=5. 13 points. Is this an intended feature? Was Patron or Fame assumed to go up to 5? I did the numbers because that particular path was easier to count then the first &quot;Adventurer&quot; path and there is already a discrepancy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27133-planguy","name":"Planguy","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"111"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-30T03:35:30-07:00","id":1465882,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Planguy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1362003-ask-a-dev?p=1465880#post1465880\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The &amp;quot;Life of Privilege&amp;quot; origin path has only 13 points worth of Edges. Fame=3, Patron=3, Skilled Liar=2, Wealth=5. 13 points. Is this an intended feature? Was Patron or Fame assumed to go up to 5? I did the numbers because that particular path was easier to count then the first &amp;quot;Adventurer&amp;quot; path and there is already a discrepancy.</div> </div> </div> </div>There are some that just missed minor bits and pieces. Find another 2 dots of Edges that say \u2018Life of Privilege\u2019 to you and chalk it up to being the first book in a brand new game line with a new system.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-30T09:03:11-07:00","id":1465904,"title":"","content":"Is there an errata available or possibly available in the future? Like as a free online supplement or perhaps a small section in an expansion?<br /> <br /> Also I really feel like the super science rules are not detailed. Apologies, I don't have my book with me at the moment so I'm operating on memory but we know that we can effectively build 3 types or tiers of super science creations. Well Talents can make 2, they can't build powered tech. Anyways I don't think we get any indication of exact rules for the actual creation process? An extrapolation of mundane tech created as super science counts as 1 scale higher, and something like a freeze gun is scale 2 and can't be mass produced. But what exactly is the difference when I'm rolling the dice?<br /> <br /> Edit<br /> <br /> Oh yeah. Do Superiors get detected by the Talent Gift &quot;Spot the Halo&quot;? They don't have a Source. Would they show up as blank? Or does the fact that they are sort of stunted Novas or Psions mean that they would still come up as odd to someone with &quot;Spot the Halo&quot;?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":27133,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27133-planguy","user":"Planguy","date":". 11-01-2021, 09:44 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27133-planguy","name":"Planguy","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"111"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-02T14:44:13-07:00","id":1466335,"title":"","content":"Hi there! Given the new Tasty Bits: Pets supplement for Aeon, with pets working like antagonists with primary, secondary, and desperation pools: How do Augendis powers work on them (which do have rules &quot;only&quot; for PC attributes and skills)? I want my Vitakinetic to boost his pet on a constant basis. Toughest and strongest ferret in the universe! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3122-shuragil","name":"shuragil","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"41"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-22T17:30:23-08:00","id":1468640,"title":"","content":"Is there a version of Nova that isn't jumped stared by Divas Mal ala the Psiad? To clarify I'm building a Nova for a game consisting of a Psiad, a Talent, and a Nova. I was looked for a rules for Dark Star Nova's which seem to be what I was looking for but couldn't find anything in the book except some notes about lowering the points to spend. Is the difference between a Nova and a Dark Star just the amount of points you spend during character creation or is it a more profound change like the Psiad/Psion difference?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27184-darrendalca","name":"DarrenDalca","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27184_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"31"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-22T21:24:07-08:00","id":1468657,"title":"","content":"<i>Psions </i>are artificially created psi-users, <i>psiads </i>are naturally-occurring.<br /> <br /> Likewise with quantum-users:<br /> <br /> <i>Superiors</i> are artificially created quantum-users, <i>novas</i> are naturally-occurring.<br /> <br /> The environmental conditions that paved the way for novas to erupt were artificially generated, but the eruption process itself happened on its own.<br /> <br /> Superiors are covered in the \u00c6on \u00c6xpansion.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#800000\">Ian A. A. Watson</span></b><span style=\"color:#bdc3c7\">(he/she)</span><br /> <b>Onyx Path Community Manager<br /> Trinity Continuum Content Lead</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4-ianwatson","name":"IanWatson","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4_2.png","title":"Community Manager","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1512"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-23T01:25:27-08:00","id":1468666,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>IanWatson</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1362003-ask-a-dev?p=1468657#post1468657\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><i>Psions </i>are artificially created psi-users, <i>psiads </i>are naturally-occurring.<br /> <br /> Likewise with quantum-users:<br /> <br /> <i>Superiors</i> are artificially created quantum-users, <i>novas</i> are naturally-occurring.<br /> <br /> The environmental conditions that paved the way for novas to erupt were artificially generated, but the eruption process itself happened on its own.<br /> <br /> Superiors are covered in the \u00c6on \u00c6xpansion.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Thank you for that, as that answers a question I hadn't gotten around to asking yet but that my group has been debating hotly since \u00c6on \u00c6xpansion came out.<br /> So based on that Dark Star Novas are mechanically the same as other Novas, just with either a lower point pool for character creation or selecting powers that are easily hidden?<br /> <br /> On a tangent related to your previous answer: For Quantum there are Natural Novas and Artificial Superiors, Psi has Natural Psiads and Artificial Psions. For Flux we've seen Natural Talents. Are there Artificial Talents? Or is that what Assassins is?<br /> <br /> (Edited out a question as it was answered earlier in the thread and I missed it first time through.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":27184,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27184-darrendalca","user":"DarrenDalca","date":". 11-23-2021, 07:46 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27184-darrendalca","name":"DarrenDalca","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27184_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"31"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-23T15:49:27-08:00","id":1468709,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DarrenDalca</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1362003-ask-a-dev?p=1468666#post1468666\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Thank you for that, as that answers a question I hadn't gotten around to asking yet but that my group has been debating hotly since \u00c6on \u00c6xpansion came out.<br /> So based on that Dark Star Novas are mechanically the same as other Novas, just with either a lower point pool for character creation or selecting powers that are easily hidden?</div> </div> </div> </div>Dark Stars are novas who are not obviously novas. Like if you've got mega-intelligence, that's not as obvious as being able to lift cars or shoot lasers. The point total doesn't really factor into it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> On a tangent related to your previous answer: For Quantum there are Natural Novas and Artificial Superiors, Psi has Natural Psiads and Artificial Psions. For Flux we've seen Natural Talents. Are there Artificial Talents? Or is that what Assassins is?<br /> </div> </div> </div>There are, as yet, no artificial Talents.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#800000\">Ian A. A. Watson</span></b><span style=\"color:#bdc3c7\">(he/she)</span><br /> <b>Onyx Path Community Manager<br /> Trinity Continuum Content Lead</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4-ianwatson","name":"IanWatson","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4_2.png","title":"Community Manager","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1512"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-03T11:08:26-08:00","id":1469511,"title":"","content":"Some of the mega attributes grants dots equal to its rating to spend on certain edges. I'm probably been dumb but for instance say you have mega intelligence 3 do you have only 3 dots total to spend or are the points cumulative which the previous ratings and you have 6 dots all together.<br /> example:<br /> mega intelligence 1 = 1 dot <br /> mega intelligence 2 = 2 dots<br /> mega intelligence 3 = 3 dots<br /> = 6 dots total<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26058-aeonstorm","name":"Aeonstorm","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-04T19:15:58-08:00","id":1469613,"title":"","content":"In the jumpstart A Quantum Leap, was Twenty-nine Eleven supposed to have stats? I haven\u2019t been able to find them if so.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/565-therian","name":"Therian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar565_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"311"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-04T19:48:39-08:00","id":1469616,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Therian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1362003-ask-a-dev?p=1469613#post1469613\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In the jumpstart A Quantum Leap, was Twenty-nine Eleven supposed to have stats? I haven\u2019t been able to find them if so.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, you're not intended to enter into combat with him, so he has no available stats. That's what the mutants are for.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#800000\">Ian A. A. Watson</span></b><span style=\"color:#bdc3c7\">(he/she)</span><br /> <b>Onyx Path Community Manager<br /> Trinity Continuum Content Lead</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4-ianwatson","name":"IanWatson","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4_2.png","title":"Community Manager","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1512"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-04T19:57:15-08:00","id":1469617,"title":"","content":"Also what is the benefit to using xp to switch your approach?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/565-therian","name":"Therian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar565_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"311"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-06T07:27:52-08:00","id":1469729,"title":"","content":"How does quantum attack work with mega might, does it stack or do you just take whichever is highest scale and then add enhancement from quantum attack.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26058-aeonstorm","name":"Aeonstorm","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-09T07:23:12-08:00","id":1470033,"title":"","content":"What is the benefit of the camaraderie bond that isn\u2019t covered by the Enhancement stunt?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/565-therian","name":"Therian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar565_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"311"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-30T06:33:55-08:00","id":1471491,"title":"","content":"Is Greater Siam meant to include most of present day Thailand, Laos, and Cambodia? I'm working on a map for my players as the one in the book is a bit different from what is described in the setting chapter.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4270-literatzi","name":"literatzi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4270_2.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-31T16:42:30-08:00","id":1471569,"title":"","content":"If you are in a situation where getting another dot in a path would leave you maxed out in something with some points left over do you lose those points? Like if I have all my Path skills maxed out and get another dot in my Path do I just not put any points in skills or can I put the points I would have gotten in another thematically appropriate skill for my Path?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27133-planguy","name":"Planguy","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"111"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-01T12:19:52-08:00","id":1471612,"title":"","content":"The Cool Under Fire edge (TC Core pg. 65) says when purchasing the Dive for Cover stunt the character gains an extra Dodge. This seems like a relic of an earlier iteration of the rules, but I'm not sure what the intent is. When Diving to Cover should they get a free level of the Dodge stunt?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4270-literatzi","name":"literatzi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4270_2.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-01T17:42:29-08:00","id":1471638,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>literatzi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1362003-ask-a-dev?p=1471491#post1471491\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is Greater Siam meant to include most of present day Thailand, Laos, and Cambodia? I'm working on a map for my players as the one in the book is a bit different from what is described in the setting chapter.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, I believe so.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-01T17:43:54-08:00","id":1471639,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Planguy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1362003-ask-a-dev?p=1471569#post1471569\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you are in a situation where getting another dot in a path would leave you maxed out in something with some points left over do you lose those points? Like if I have all my Path skills maxed out and get another dot in my Path do I just not put any points in skills or can I put the points I would have gotten in another thematically appropriate skill for my Path?</div> </div> </div> </div>I don\u2019t believe the rules specifically cover this, but Storypath isn\u2019t in the habit of stealing points from characters or depowering player choices. If I were the SG in this instance I\u2019d let the player spend the additional points on thematically appropriate skills, as you\u2019ve suggested.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-08T14:42:12-08:00","id":1472087,"title":"","content":"(Aberrant p.204) Can I apply the &quot;Variable(X)&quot; tag to a Technique?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1001-timecrafter","name":"Timecrafter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1001_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"134"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-16T22:15:29-08:00","id":1472606,"title":"","content":"Can Bestow/Impose be used to put the effects of a power onto objects and not just people?<br /> <br /> For example, is it possible to give Quantum Aura power the Impose power tag in order to make <i>something</i> (instead of just <i>someone</i>) dangerous to touch?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26905-eternl-knight","name":"Eternl Knight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26905_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"106"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-19T18:18:20-08:00","id":1472833,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eternl Knight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1362003-ask-a-dev?p=1472606#post1472606\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can Bestow/Impose be used to put the effects of a power onto objects and not just people?<br /> <br /> For example, is it possible to give Quantum Aura power the Impose power tag in order to make <i>something</i> (instead of just <i>someone</i>) dangerous to touch?</div> </div> </div> </div>Bestow requires the subject to be able to control the power, so I\u2019d say no to that one (but only for that reason). Impose is under the control of the nova, so I don\u2019t see any reason why not. <br /> <br /> Even if the ST decides that RAW dictates no to both, there\u2019s no reason that a character couldn\u2019t have the equivalent for inanimate objects only.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-22T11:58:41-08:00","id":1473038,"title":"","content":"I really loved the way they managed to add scale, while some scales where added by the original rules (naming size and speed, mainly).<br /> <br /> But it is not totally clear if this increase in scale could be added to the maximum scale of size for example.<br /> <br /> Let\u2019s say a PK wants to fly faster, it\u2019s possible to go up to (check Aeon) mode dots (or half for space speed). They can the scales from both sources (regular rules and PU) stack?<br /> <br /> Making it a bit more solid, PK has Psi 4 and Telekinesis 5, they could manage to reach Speed 5 with only 1 success (regular speed), or 6 spending one extra success. Using their rule, they could add further 4 (supposing they get something like 9 extra successes). The question is not about being possible to reach scale 9, the question is about can the scales stack in this case?<br /> <br /> I know it\u2019s not the focus of this rules, it\u2019s more about the scales that where described in the rules (number of targets, power and durability, intensity, etc)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-06T21:38:07-08:00","id":1474106,"title":"","content":"As a general question about the Continuum, is traveling from one worldline in the continuum to another going to be solely the province of the Inspired/Talents?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26448,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26448-shalmaneser","user":"Shalmaneser","date":". 02-07-2022, 06:09 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26448-shalmaneser","name":"Shalmaneser","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"79"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-08T02:58:53-08:00","id":1474179,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shalmaneser</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1362003-ask-a-dev?p=1474106#post1474106\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As a general question about the Continuum, is traveling from one worldline in the continuum to another going to be solely the province of the Inspired/Talents?</div> </div> </div> </div>Not necessarily. There's probably going to be an Inspired involved somewhere in there, as breaching dimensions is probably a super-science invention at best. But there's plenty of precedent in shows like <i>Sliders</i> where a variety of characters are jumping to alternate universes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#800000\">Ian A. A. Watson</span></b><span style=\"color:#bdc3c7\">(he/she)</span><br /> <b>Onyx Path Community Manager<br /> Trinity Continuum Content Lead</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4-ianwatson","name":"IanWatson","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4_2.png","title":"Community Manager","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1512"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-26T22:14:13-08:00","id":1475518,"title":"","content":"If humans eventually &quot;persuade&quot; a Doyen to part with the secrets of the Prometheus chamber and make one without the one-Aptitude limitation, what's the most likely outcome? Would it be the Doyen-equivalent one at 7+others at 5 or something unique to humanity?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26448-shalmaneser","name":"Shalmaneser","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"79"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-27T02:19:34-08:00","id":1475525,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shalmaneser</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1362003-ask-a-dev?p=1475518#post1475518\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If humans eventually &quot;persuade&quot; a Doyen to part with the secrets of the Prometheus chamber and make one without the one-Aptitude limitation, what's the most likely outcome? Would it be the Doyen-equivalent one at 7+others at 5 or something unique to humanity?</div> </div> </div> </div>That\u2019s far too speculative to be a dev question. Go answer those questions for your own game.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-17T17:26:56-07:00","id":1476612,"title":"","content":"Can I ask what buying extra dots in <b>Digital Manipulation</b> (Mega-Edge: 12pts per dot) is meant to do when the only benefit given is substituting for <b>Intellect</b> (Attribute: 10pts per dot) or <b>Technology</b> (Skill: 5pts per dot) in the Intellect+Technology roll to activate/use the power. It is straight up better mathematically to just buy the one dot of Mega-Edge and pay XP to improve Intellect/Technology instead. Was there something cut out of the power in editing?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26905-eternl-knight","name":"Eternl Knight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26905_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"106"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-26T18:24:47-07:00","id":1477496,"title":"","content":"While re-reading the super-science rules for \u00c6on, I found this nugget :<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The Rank 6 items that Tier 3 psions can create are described in a later supplement. </div> </div> </div>From what I recall of the Monday Meeting Notes, I thought that (sadly) the only things left in the works for the \u00c6on era were novels.<br /> <br /> Is there a (or several) sourcebook(s) in the works, or is this referring to another book that's already out ?<br /> <br /> Thanks !","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26426-trianoma4evah","name":"Trianoma4Evah","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"27"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-26T22:23:08-07:00","id":1477520,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Trianoma4Evah</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1362003-ask-a-dev?p=1477496#post1477496\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">While re-reading the super-science rules for \u00c6on, I found this nugget :<br /> <br /> From what I recall of the Monday Meeting Notes, I thought that (sadly) the only things left in the works for the \u00c6on era were novels.<br /> <br /> Is there a (or several) sourcebook(s) in the works, or is this referring to another book that's already out ?<br /> <br /> Thanks !</div> </div> </div> </div>It\u2019s not in any supplement so far, but that doesn\u2019t mean it won\u2019t ever happen. As for what books are coming for Aeon, you may be confusing the Kickstarter fulfilment with general supplement production. The Kickstarter has successfully released all achieved products, with the last being the novels. Aeon itself has had a healthy post-Kickstarter life with many supplements released. <i>Mission Statements</i>, the organizations sourcebook, is still in the production pipeline at the moment. Other TC lines are getting more products as well and there are only so many writers/artists/developers to pull it all together.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-26T21:42:36-07:00","id":1482056,"title":"","content":"So, somebody on Page 6 already asked this question but since no one answered and I'm wondering the same thing, I guess I'll ask that question too.<br /> <br /> On page 104 of the Core Rulebook,the <b>Establish Grapple</b> stunt states that its Success cost is &quot;Variable.&quot;<br /> The Grappled rules on the same page state that breaking a grapple is an opposed roll, with no mention of an established Successes cost or modifier or anything.<br /> <br /> Soooooo, how much does the Establish Grapple stunt cost? I know in Scion 2E it sets the Difficulty of breaking the Grapple, but that's not how it works in this game.<br /> <br /> Bonus question: Why is there no combined Errata document? That would be really convenient.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1964-the-voice","name":"The Voice","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"27"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-28T17:04:43-07:00","id":1482203,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Voice</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1362003-ask-a-dev?p=1482056#post1482056\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On page 104 of the Core Rulebook,the <b>Establish Grapple</b> stunt states that its Success cost is &amp;quot;Variable.&amp;quot;<br /> The Grappled rules on the same page state that breaking a grapple is an opposed roll, with no mention of an established Successes cost or modifier or anything.<br /> <br /> Soooooo, how much does the Establish Grapple stunt cost? I know in Scion 2E it sets the Difficulty of breaking the Grapple, but that's not how it works in this game.</div> </div> </div> </div>Grapple is effectively a 0 cost stunt. If you overcome your opponent\u2019s Defense, you can fling your limbs around them and initiate the grapple. This essentially locks you and them into a mini game where you\u2019re moving or dragging each other around, or breaking free.<br /> <br /> Edit to add: I should note that this doesn't preclude various characters/creatures having specific features that make Grapple harder, hence the 'Variable' aspect. A slime covered creature may increase the difficulty of any grappling attempts by 2, by way of example, which would make the Grappling stunt cost an additional 2 successes over Defense, if you wanted to buy it. Similarly, an aberrant may have a phase shift power that makes physical objects slide through them, or a frictionless mutation which makes them nearly impossible to grasp.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":156,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","user":"Bunyip","date":". 05-30-2022, 02:08 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-19T21:14:51-07:00","id":1484471,"title":"","content":"Re: Aeon. The Level 2 Transmassion power Relay Person permits a resistance roll to avoid being involuntarily teleported. The Level 4 Transmit Person doesn't have one in the description- is the target simply out of luck?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26448-shalmaneser","name":"Shalmaneser","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"79"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-22T18:23:29-07:00","id":1484736,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shalmaneser</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1362003-ask-a-dev?p=1484471#post1484471\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Re: Aeon. The Level 2 Transmassion power Relay Person permits a resistance roll to avoid being involuntarily teleported. The Level 4 Transmit Person doesn't have one in the description- is the target simply out of luck?</div> </div> </div> </div>You\u2019ll need to exercise some SG discretion on these cases. Firstly, Transmassion 2 doesn\u2019t allow a \u2018resistance roll\u2019, it allows an attempt at the \u2018roll away\u2019 defense stunt. You\u2019re not resisting the jump, you\u2019re trying to get out of the teleporter\u2019s range/grasp before the port takes place. <br /> <br /> Transmassion 4 doesn\u2019t include this by default because the teleporter has to spend several rounds in intense concentration before the port occurs. So, if the unwilling \u2018victim\u2019 doesn\u2019t want to be teleported they have sufficient time to just walk away, no \u2018roll away\u2019 stunt required. But, say the victim is restrained and they spend the first of those several rounds freeing themselves, and they get free just before the teleport occurs, then certainly allow them to attempt a\u2019 roll away\u2019 defensive stunt to throw themselves clear.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-10T09:50:40-07:00","id":1492764,"title":"","content":"In Phoenix Trust, third generation psions have the duration of their powers limited to 'while attunement lasts'. I always thought that psion attunement was instant - how long does it last?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1524-pcontop","name":"pcontop","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1524_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"278"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-05T10:31:55-08:00","id":1502218,"title":"","content":"So Enviromental 2 armor tag, does it just reduce continuous damage as a whole by 4 or do you have to pick a particular source of that type of damage like fire/heat, Cold, etc? I am specifically in relation to the Quantom Field Nova power if that effects it in anyway.<br /> \u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5280-gfrobbin84","name":"gfrobbin84","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"90"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-31T00:02:11-07:00","id":1513361,"title":"","content":"So I was looking in character creation in the core book and I noticed that for path creation you choose an attribute keyword and 2 skills as keywords for what Gifts you can get. This matches up with what you find in the provided examples of Origins and Roles. But for Allegiances your keywords are three skills. I never really noticed this because you are still getting a choice of three different things, you just replace an attribute with another skill. But why do you miss out on another attribute keyword? I was trying to find where in the text a society path is different then an origin or role path, but couldn't find that information.<br /> <br /> If I was to design a unique society path for a Talent would I choose three skills keywords or an attribute keyword and two skill keywords for Gifts?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27133-planguy","name":"Planguy","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"111"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-15T01:34:16-07:00","id":1518014,"title":"","content":"Is there a list how to &quot;convert&quot; the &quot;old skills&quot; from Aeon Trinity, or Aberrant<br /> <br /> It would just help (coming from &quot;rpgs with standard skills&quot;) how to handle the skills, which are not on the list of continuum","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28098-damotil","name":"damotil","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-15T01:44:43-07:00","id":1518015,"title":"","content":"Chapter 5 in the Adventure book was supposed to have info on creating and advancing your own Allegiance as per chapter 3, page 99. But I can't seem to find anything like that? <br /> <br /> At least the Super Science rules seem more coherent then what was in the core book.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27133-planguy","name":"Planguy","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"111"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-23T20:34:32-07:00","id":1518678,"title":"","content":"Teleport, Aberrant pg. 223 states:<br /> &quot;The nova can substitute a Quantum + Teleport roll for a Dodge Stunt, applying successes an opponent must overcome in order to inflict an Injury. This costs the usual two Quantum points and the nova cannot teleport more than a single range band.&quot; <br /> <br /> Does this mean a Nova with Teleport can <u><b>only</b></u> use the above stunt to avoid an attack that inflicts an injury condition?<br /> <br /> If my teleporter is about to get hit by another Nova who aims to launch him into the stratosphere (via copious amounts of mega might and the push stunt) but importantly not inflict an injury condition, could my teleporter still use the teleport dodge stunt to Teleport out of the way of the push attack?<br /> \u200b\u200b<br /> Or to avoid a grapple?<br /> <br /> It seems like this was supposed to be a dodge replacer but the wording severely limits what you can use it against. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25261-solarknight","name":"SolarKnight","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-01T15:47:05-07:00","id":1519372,"title":"","content":"The Indomitable Will Gift (TC corebook p. 205-206) says that &quot;Those attempting to influence the mind of the character through Manipulation or a Mental power receive a Complication equal to half the character\u2019s Resolve (rounded up).\u200b&quot;<br /> <br /> It does not appear to specify what happens if the offender fails to overcome the Complication. I assume something must happen, though. What happens?<br /> <br /> Or should it just be a Difficulty increase?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11237-jefepato","name":"Jefepato","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11237_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"557"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-09T06:48:35-07:00","id":1523875,"title":"","content":"I haven't seen a straight answer to this anywhere are Superiors Paramorphs, Eximorphs, or Psychomorphs? The first two seem far more likely. The lack of Dramatic Editing makes me say Eximorph. The general similarity to an upgraded Talent makes me doubt that.<br /> <br /> Is there an official ruling on whether the Supriors are closer to Stalwarts or Daredevils?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I used to be Median but life has made me Mean.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1753-avrjoe","name":"Avrjoe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1753_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"69"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-09T06:53:12-07:00","id":1523876,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Avrjoe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1362003-ask-a-dev?p=1523875#post1523875\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I haven't seen a straight answer to this anywhere are Superiors Paramorphs, Eximorphs, or Psychomorphs? The first two seem far more likely. The lack of Dramatic Editing makes me say Eximorph. The general similarity to an upgraded Talent makes me doubt that.<br /> <br /> Is there an official ruling on whether the Supriors are closer to Stalwarts or Daredevils?</div> </div> </div> </div>Jinketsu are eximorphs. They're essentially artificially-created stalwarts.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#800000\">Ian A. A. Watson</span></b><span style=\"color:#bdc3c7\">(he/she)</span><br /> <b>Onyx Path Community Manager<br /> Trinity Continuum Content Lead</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4-ianwatson","name":"IanWatson","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4_2.png","title":"Community Manager","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1512"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-14T14:27:38-08:00","id":1530847,"title":"","content":"Any recommendations for a character changing templates? For example a Stalwart and Mesmerist lives through the Adventure age and becomes a Nova and Psiad?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I used to be Median but life has made me Mean.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1753-avrjoe","name":"Avrjoe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1753_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"69"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-14T18:27:01-08:00","id":1530858,"title":"","content":"Sorry, answered but should not\u2026","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-03-16T14:17:32-07:00","id":1549374,"title":"","content":"Aegis and Adventure both have all three types of character Paramorphs, Psychomorphs, and Eximorphs. So how do they compare? Power wise how do Champions, Oracles, and Olympians stack up to Daredevils, Mesmerists, and Stalwarts.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I used to be Median but life has made me Mean.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1753-avrjoe","name":"Avrjoe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1753_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"69"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-10-14T20:59:15-07:00","id":1564757,"title":"","content":"So, a question: In Aberrant, the Detection Mega-Edge allows you to detect living beings. Could it instead be used to detect the biological make-up of those beings? Like looking for old injuries, toxins in their blood, that sort of thing? And would that all fall under one category, or require multiple &quot;fields?&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26317-critian-caceorte","name":"Critian Caceorte","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"246"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}